window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-085", "name_zh": "直觉", "name_en": "intuition", "tagline": "赛斯说的直觉不是一种说不清的模糊感觉，而是内在感官的直接知晓：它不走一步一步的推理，常常比意识心先知道，而理智恰恰要靠它这份现成的信息库才跑得起来。", "explanation": "赛斯讲直觉，讲的不是一种神秘能力，而是心灵的第二种工作方式。理智一件一件地拆开来检查，直觉一口把整体吞下：它不受逻辑定律与因果束缚，不考虑你们所知的连续性时间，所以能「来不及想就知道」（第44、215节）。他给的定位很清楚——直觉是内在感官的一条接收通道，通向那个比意识心大得多的自己，里面装着你迫切需要的知识、直觉与记忆（第23、31节）。他跟「理智」那一页的分工在这里划开：那一页说这件工具怎么用、极限在哪儿；这一页说它的地基——知性的推演不必只靠自己那点知识，它要靠直觉那庞大的神奇信息库，而所有知性的信息本来都从那里涌出（《神奇之道》第12节）。所以他既不是要你用直觉取代理智，也不是要理智压住直觉，而是反复要那个「自律但直觉」的组合：自我不必退场，但必须暂时挪开，否则它会把自己变成直觉自己的监狱（第308、88节）。他也老实给出刻度：直觉通常可信，不是永远可信，它会把正确的感觉放错地方，而人会把它合理化掉（第19、10、514节）。他还说这件事与身体连在一起——直觉看似精神，其实也是行动，会改动肉体的化学与电磁层面，也参与治疗与创造（第198、803节）。最要紧的一条是给普通读者的：这些资料直觉上本该能接到大部分，读它要用心智和你自己的直觉一起用（第883节）。", "definitions": [{"zh": "直觉不受所谓的逻辑定律以及因-果关系的束缚。它们并没有把你们知道的时间列入考虑，因此它们不受连续性的束缚，也不受限于一个接着一个的言语文字或甚至是思想的沟通。", "en": "The intuitions are not bound by the so-called laws of logic, and cause and effect. They do not take time as you know it into consideration, therefore they are not bound by continuity or limited to communication of words or even thoughts, strung out one after another.", "source": "Session 44"}, {"zh": "逻辑（Logic）一步步地建立它的典范，一个想法接着一个想法，一连串的想法或推演是依赖前一个想法。直觉有一个更自发的本质，较不依赖如此一步接着一步的推演过程。", "en": "Logic builds its monuments step by step, one thought before the other in a series where each thought or deduction is dependent upon the thought before. The intuitions are of a more spontaneous nature, and less dependent upon such step-by-step movements.", "source": "Session 215"}, {"zh": "逻辑是处理外在的状况，处理因果关系，而直觉是处理最亲密的切身经验，处理以你们的话来说移动得远比光速还快的主观运动与活动，以及处理你们的因果层面因为太慢而感知不到的同时性事件。", "en": "Logic deals with exterior conditions, with cause-and-effect relationships. Intuitions deal with immediate experience of the most intimate nature, with subjective motions and activities that in your terms move far quicker than the speed of light, and with simultaneous events that your cause-and-effect level is far too slow to perceive.", "source": "Session 803"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "直觉是什么：不推理，直接就知道", "note": "赛斯给直觉下的定义从来不是一种说不清的感觉，而是一种不同的处理方式。他说直觉不受所谓逻辑定律与因果关系的束缚，也没把你们知道的时间列入考虑，因此不受连续性限制，也不受限于「一个接着一个的言语文字或甚至是思想的沟通」（第44节）。区别在做法：逻辑是一座一层一层堆起来的纪念碑，每一个推演都依赖前面那一个；直觉的本性更自发，不走这种一步步的动作（第215节）。同一节他把分工说得很整齐——自我把行动越拆越小以便检查，直觉试着感知行动的整体；自我在分解，直觉在组成。最反直觉的是第197节那句：自我不能像直觉的自己那样即时做决定，所以它几乎用慢动作来感知事件，整体效果就变成一件接一件、有先有后。也就是说，来不及想就知道，靠的不是玄，是两套工具本来就在两种速度上工作。第180节他给了个比喻收尾：好奇的直觉与爱追根究底的自己像夏日的风，能在大小空间里旅行，知道比针头还小、比银河还大的现状。", "src": "《早期课》第2册第44节；第5册第215节；第4册第197、180节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 215 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 197 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 180 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0044", "zh": "这个资料，实际上并不像它看起来的那么难以理解。你们应该在直觉上，会理解它的大部分。直觉不受所谓的逻辑定律以及因-果关系的束缚。它们并没有把你们知道的时间列入考虑，因此它们不受连续性的束缚，也不受限于一个接着一个的言语文字或甚至是思想的沟通。", "en": "This material is actually not nearly as difficult to understand as it may seem. Intuitively you should pick up much of it. The intuitions are not bound by the so-called laws of logic, and cause and effect. They do not take time as you know it into consideration, therefore they are not bound by continuity or limited to communication of words or even thoughts, strung out one after another.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0158", "zh": "逻辑（Logic）一步步地建立它的典范，一个想法接着一个想法，一连串的想法或推演是依赖前一个想法。直觉有一个更自发的本质，较不依赖如此一步接着一步的推演过程。", "en": "Logic builds its monuments step by step, one thought before the other in a series where each thought or deduction is dependent upon the thought before. The intuitions are of a more spontaneous nature, and less dependent upon such step-by-step movements.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第215节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "215", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0159", "zh": "自我试图把行动分解为更小的单位。直觉试着感知行动的整体。自我是为了检验的目的而分解，而直觉是组成。自我和直觉都在执行它们的功能，很明显地创造了行动。自己当然可能以一种行动的完形来考虑，由它自己不同的层面以不同的方式来感知。", "en": "The ego attempts to break down action into smaller and smaller units. The intuitions try to perceive action as a whole. The ego breaks down for purposes of examination, the intuitions construct. Both the ego and the intuitions, in performing their functions, obviously create action. The self may of course be considered as a gestalt of action, perceived in a different manner by various levels of itself.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第215节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "215", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0148", "zh": "自我会以很强的辨识力，选择接收的管道；也会检查任何它觉得对自己的主控权带来威胁的事物。然而，在睡眠中许多的梦都具有心电感应的特质，也强烈带有千里眼的意味。自我在选择要对何种刺激予以回应时，会采行一贯的辨识标准，正是这种辨识标准，大幅决定了呈现在人格面前的物理时间本质。由于自我的功能和基本特质，所以无法像直觉的自己（intuitive self）那样可以即使做决定。因此，它以一种特别的方式感知事件，几乎是用慢动作，于是整体效果变成是一连串彼此分开的事件，按先后顺序一件一件发生。", "en": "The ego chooses channels of reception with great discrimination; and, again, it censors anything which it feels is a threat to its own dominance. In sleep however many dreams are of a telepathic nature, with strong clairvoyant overtones. It is the ego’s persistent discrimination in choosing the stimuli to which it will react that in a large measure determines the nature of physical time as it appears to the personality. The ego, because of its function and basic characteristics, cannot make swift decisions as can the intuitive self. Therefore it perceives events in a peculiar manner, almost in slow motion, so that the whole effect is of a series of separate events, one happening before or after the other.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第197节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "197", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0141", "zh": "好奇的直觉和喜好追根究底的自己，就像夏日的风一样，可以旅行在大大小小的空间，可以了解各种比针头还小、比银河还大的现状。", "en": "The inquiring intuitions and the searching self, like summer winds, can travel in small and large spaces, can know of actualities that are more minute than pinheads and more massive than galaxies.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第180节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "180", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "它比意识心先知道，还常常绕道梦来", "note": "来自内我的讯息如果够强就跨得过意识的屏障，但这类直觉通常先以梦的形式出现，稍后才显现在自我面前；很多讯息是提前放在梦里的，等到情况有需要时才释放给意识心（第93节）。同一节他还补了一句常被忽略的话：意识心消化吸收「直觉牢记在心的知识」，速度极慢——所以你常常已经知道，只是还没想通。他不把它当比喻，而是当生存机能：在梦中出现的直觉被记住、在清醒时被利用，因而保证了意识的机动与肉体的幸存（《灵魂永生》第532节）。为什么要绕道梦？因为新的可能性与直觉的解决必须在梦里出现，人的学习才不至于只靠一个不许创造性资料进来的反馈系统（《心灵的本质》第792节）；而梦里的创造行为不只是直觉地建立，也是用一种远超过你们对「逻辑」这个字的理解所形成的逻辑组织起来的（第795节）。落到日常就很好认：一个在梦中给出的判断，可能要过一阵才换了形式来到你意识前——以预感、突然的直觉，或一股行动的冲动（《个人实相的本质》第670节）；同时的自己的那些冒险，也会以痕迹、白日梦、断裂的意象或突然的直觉出现（第669节）。《早期课》第9册第468节讲了最省事的一种：那个埋在过去的结浮到意识的光亮里，是因为在内里，直觉早已把必要的联结通通接通了。", "src": "《早期课》第3册第93节；第9册第468节；《灵魂永生》第532节；《心灵的本质》第792、795节；《个人实相的本质》第669、670节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 93 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 468 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 532 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 792 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 795 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 669 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 670 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0093", "zh": "如果来自内我的讯息够强，就会跨越意识障碍，有意识的自我接收到它们简直乐透了。但这样的直觉通常先以梦的形式出现，稍后才显现于自我面前；而且很多这样的讯息提前出现在梦中，在情况有需要时才释放到意识心智。", "en": "Messages from the inner self if strong enough will pass through the conscious barriers, and the conscious ego is only too happy to receive them. But such intuitions have usually first appeared in dream form, appearing to the ego later; and many such messages appear in dreams ahead of time, to be released to the conscious mind when situations demand it.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第93节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "93", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0096", "zh": "它不像你想像的那么重要，因为往往你自动更有智慧地行事，意识心消化吸收直觉牢记在心的知识，速度极慢。", "en": "It is not as important as you may think, since oftentimes you act with more wisdom automatically, and the conscious mind is extremely slow to assimilate knowledge that the intuitions know by heart.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第93节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "93", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0377", "zh": "这导致了意识的机动性，的确进而保证了他的肉体的幸存，他也记得那些在他梦中出现的直觉，而在清醒时加以利用。", "en": "This resulted in a mobility of consciousness that indeed insured his physical survival, and those intuitions that appeared to him in the dream state were remembered and taken advantage of in the waking state.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第532节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "532", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0528", "zh": "不过，如果这真的是如此，那么人类的历史将永远不会有任何真的改变。替代的经验路径——新的可能性与直觉的解决——经常在梦境出现，以使人的学习不仅只依赖一个不容许填入创造性数据的回馈系统。做梦于是提供人类除此之外得不到的学习经验。在梦中，能以比传统日常实相更为发展的、更高的了解来评判行为与事件。", "en": "If this were really the case, however, mankind’s history would never change in any true regard. Alternate paths of experience — new possibilities and intuitive solutions — constantly appear in the dream state, so that man’s learning is not simply dependent upon a feedback system that does not allow for the insertion of creative material. Dreaming then provides the species with learning experience not otherwise available, in which behavior and events can be judged against more developed and higher understanding than that present in conventional daily reality at any level.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第792节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "792", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0529", "zh": "因为你们对逻辑的概念非常狭隘，在你看来，好像做梦的自己是不会判断的，或不合“逻辑的”。然而，它却以惊人的辨识力工作，筛检数据，把一些送到身体的某部分，并构成记忆。安眠药也阻碍了梦的判断机能，那是经常被忽略的。事实是，梦涉及了高度的创造行为。这些不仅是直觉地建立的，还是以远超过你对逻辑的概念的逻辑形成的。然后这些创造性行为透过联想过程彼此拼合，极精确地连结在一起，以形成梦的事件。", "en": "Because you have very limited ideas of what logic is, it seems to you that the dreaming self is not critical, or “logical”; yet it works with amazing discrimination, sifting data, sending some to certain portions of the body, and structuring memory. Sleeping pills also impede the critical functions of dreams that are so often overlooked. The facts are that dreams involve high acts of creativity. These are not only intuitively based, but formed with a logic far surpassing your ideas of that quality. These creative acts are then fitted together through associative processes that come together most precisely to form the dream events.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第795节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "795", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0451", "zh": "以实质的说法来说，可能要花些时间，你的意识心才会接受或认知梦中所给的诊断。它可能稍后以不同的形式，好比说，以一个预感、突然的直觉，或冲动的行动时来到。 如果你不信任自己，可能会忽略这种动力或没有好好地利用那些答案。", "en": "Now, in physical terms it may take some time before your conscious mind accepts or recognizes a diagnosis given in a dream. It may come to you later in altered form as a hunch or sudden intuition, or an urge for action. If you do not trust yourself you may ignore such impetuses and not take advantage of the answers.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第670节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "670", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0449", "zh": "再次地，你“同时的自己”的探险，在你的意识里会出现为“痕迹”、意念、白日梦或不连贯的意象，有时候甚至为突然的直觉。它们可以被汲取、被拉出来以帮助你了解目前的问题。", "en": "The adventures of your simultaneous selves, again, appear as traces in your own consciousness, as ideas or daydreams or disconnected images, or sometimes even in sudden intuitions. They can be drawn upon, drawn out, to help you understand current problems.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第669节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "669", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0337", "zh": "因为这些课，你们两位都变了许许多多。直觉上、创造上，新的通道都会向你们打开。然而这并不是非此即彼的处境。鲁柏不必用苦哈哈的责任感去想问题。（停顿。）而此刻他不再这样了。今晚，出于好几个原因，他在这几件事上想通了。那个多少埋藏在过去的结，也浮到了意识的光亮里，因为在内里，直觉早已把必要的联结通通接通了。", "en": "You have both greatly changed as a result of the sessions. Intuitively and creatively new avenues will be opened to you. There is no either/or situation however. Ruburt need not think in terms of grim responsibility. (Pause.) And now he will not. This evening for several reasons his thoughts became clear on these subjects. And the point, buried somewhat in the past, came to light of consciousness, for within intuitively the necessary connections had already been made.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第468节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "468", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "理智是骑在直觉上跑的", "note": "这一页和「理智」那一页的分界就在这里：那页讲理智这件工具怎么用、边界在哪儿，这页讲它的地基。赛斯说得非常直白——你期待知性去做推演，却同时剥夺它应有的那份安慰：它的推演不必只靠自己那点知识，而可以依靠直觉那庞大的神奇信息库；以更大的说法，所有知性的信息都必须从那里涌出（《神奇之道》第12节）。同一本书第6节他说人正是被教去埋没知性做好本职工作所依赖的那套直觉能力，因为知性必须回头跟自己感受的部分核对，取回馈、取支持、取对身体状况的知识；拿不到回馈，它只能在原地疯狂空转。《早期课》第4册第197节给了演化式的解释：事件看起来分开成一件一件，是为了训练理性，否则一切都靠直觉来用，理性就不会发展——那道墙是理智的练习场，不是实相的样子。第165节他说这种对人格的了解根本不能循合乎逻辑的路线；理性确实能从直觉手里拿到一些讯息，但它自己只觉察到整个人格极细微的部分，而他特别说明这不是要贬低理性的价值。第100节给的是流水线顺序：理智一旦觉察到直觉或内我交给它的资料，就有能力通知自我，自我随即改变态度，这样全才不必自己跟自己打架。《灵魂永生》第546节他要求理性与情感、直觉携手同行，否则新得到自由的意识会抓住理性关于实相的概念，而拒认自己真正身处其中的那个实相。两派都错：一派认定意识心与理性拥有全部答案，一派认定答案都在情绪里；最大的谬误是认为知觉最重要的作用必须是分析性的，而不是去理解与消化直觉的心灵知识（《个人实相的本质》第638节）。第825节他补了直觉自己的组织方式：它跟想象力一样靠联想，把不同的东西统一起来，那种统一常常不受因果的限制。最后他说清了自己要什么：他一直在讲直觉与推理能力之间的平衡，希望引领两者结合——那结合在你们的世界里会显成像一种全新的官能，把两边最好的成分合在一起，而两边都被不可计量地加强（《梦、进化与价值完成》第914节）。顺序他也讲过：早期人类更认同自己直觉的那一面和想象力，由这两样去指挥知性用在何处（《神奇之道》第15节）；把内在知识实际用起来是知性的活儿，于是直觉与知性手携手合作（第17节）。", "src": "《神奇之道》第12、6、15、17节；《早期课》第4册第197、165节；第3册第100节；《灵魂永生》第546节；《个人实相的本质》第638、825节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第914节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 12 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 6 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 15 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 17 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 197 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 165 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 100 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 546 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 638 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 825 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 914 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "知性用的资料本来就来自直觉", "note": "赛斯不是说理智没用，而是说它运作的原料不由它自己生产。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0605", "zh": "当然，我还有更多要说的，希望那能让你们以一种清楚的方式用你们的知性，并改进你们的作为。再次的，你们若说「在这情况里——或在任何情况里——不可能为我的知性所知的元素」，是相当正确的，因此，知性能考虑那个事实。不然的话，你们期待知性去推理，同时却否定了它应有的安慰，那即是，知道它并不需要只靠它的知识去做推理，却还可依赖直觉广大的神奇信息库藏——以较大的说法，就是所有的知性信息都必须由此涌出。所以我认为你俩最终都在那方向上用到了新的处理方式。", "en": "I will, of course, have more to say that will hopefully allow you to use your intellects in a clear fashion, to better your performances. You are quite right, again, to say that “There are elements in this situation — or in any given situation — impossible for my intellect to know,” so the intellect can take that fact into consideration. Otherwise, you expect it to make deductions while denying it the comfort it should have, of knowing that its deductions need not be made on its own knowledge alone, but on the intuition’s vast magical bank of information — from which, in larger terms, all of the intellect’s information must spring. So I think you are both finally trying to use a new approach in that direction.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第12节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "12", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0596", "zh": "你被教以去埋没知性，为了要做它该做的工作所需的直觉能力本身——因为知性必须与自己的感受部分查核，以得到回馈、支持，以及对于生物性状况的知识。不给它那种回馈时，知性可能会在疯狂的试车时，停在原地打转。（停顿良久。）在每一刻，从最微细的层面，身体对于（停顿）它在物质实相内的位置，多少都经常有个确定的画面。 事实上，那张画面是由亿万个不断变化的较小快照——或不如说动画——组成的，决定那么多的状况、位置和图像，以至于它们永远无法被描述。在任意一个特定片刻，你结果拥有了一张占优势的实相画面——那是心理、生理和电磁阶层活动的结果。一张画面被置换在其它画面上，而不断在做的计算，使得所有组成物质存在的组合物相遇、交会，以给你生命。", "en": "You are taught to submerge the very intuitive abilities that the intellect needs to do its proper work — for the intellect must check with the feeling portions of the self for feedback, for support, for knowledge as to biological conditions. Denied that feedback, it can spin on endlessly in frenzied dry runs. (Long pause.) At each moment, from the most microscopic levels the body (pause) in one way or another is ascertaining a constant picture of its position within physical reality. That picture is composed of millions of ever-changing smaller snapshots, as it were — or moving pictures is better — determining so many conditions, positions and relationships that they could never be described. You end up with a predominating picture of reality in any given moment — one that is the result of the activity of psychological, biological, and electromagnetic stratas. One picture is transposed upon the others, and calculations made constantly, so that all of the components that make up physical existence are met, and intersect to give you life.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第6节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "6", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0105", "zh": "然而，自我并不是和全我失去连结的一个后来添加的东西，当理智觉察到直觉或内我给它的资料时，它就有能力通知自我，接着自我便可据以改变它的态度。这样一来我们就能确定全我的合作，避免分裂一个自己，自己的一部分与另一部分对抗的任何可能性。", "en": "The ego however is not an afterthought disconnected from the whole self, and when the intellect becomes aware of data given to it by the intuitions or the inner self, it is then capable of informing the ego, which then changes its attitude accordingly. This way we are assured of the cooperation of the whole self, and avoid any possibility of splitting one self, one part of the self, against another.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第100节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "100", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0133", "zh": "这样的了解完全不能遵循合逻辑的路线。理性或许真的可以从直觉中掌握到一些讯息，但理性本身只能觉察整个人格的一些细微部分。这么说并不是要贬低理性的价值，事实依然是，人格所追寻的答案，只能在组成自己的那些行动之内全面搜寻，才能找得到。我在上一节课曾解释过，有一些基本的心理资产就存在于人格的行动结构当中，这个资产不会流失，而且极其重要，要是没有它，就无法建立起人格系统。", "en": "Such understanding simply cannot follow logical lines. The intellect may indeed grasp some of this understanding from the intuitions, but the intellect itself is aware of only minute portions of the whole personality. Again, this is not meant to minimize the value of the intellect. The fact remains that answers sought by a personality can only be found through a traveling within the actions that compose the self. Within our last session, I explained some of the basic psychological heritage that resides within the action makeup of the personality. There is no escaping this heritage, and it is so important that without it the personality system could not be built up.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第165节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "165", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0383", "zh": "它们是极端的表面化，大半是误用智性能力的结果。光凭智能无法了解直觉所最确切知道的东西。智能为了试图使人世生活对它而言有意义，乃设立了这些对比与敌对的因素。智能说：“如果有善，必有恶。”因为它要干净利落地解释事情。如果有上升，必然有下降。一定要有平衡。可是，内我领悟到由大得多的观点来说，恶只是无知，“上升”与“下降”只是利落的术语，被应用到不知有此种方向的空间上。", "en": "They are extremely superficial and largely the result of misused intellectual abilities. The intellect alone cannot understand what the intuitions most certainly know. In trying to make sense in its terms of physical existence, the intellect has set up these opposing factors. The intellect says, “If there is good, there must be evil,” for it wants things explained in neat parcels. If there is an up, there must be a down. There must be balance. The inner self, however, realizes that in much larger terms, evil is simply ignorance, that “up” and “down” are neat terms applied to space which knows no such directions.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第546节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "546", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "并用，不是二选一", "note": "他把理性对直觉这道选择题整个撤掉：两边各有功能，合起来才是一种新官能。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0149", "zh": "理性（intellect）是自我的一部分，它的发展很重要，而各自分开的独立事件会让理性得到训练，否则全部都依赖直觉，那理性就不会发展，因为在个体意识与本体更进一步的特别化上面，理性是个重点特征。", "en": "The intellect is a part of the ego, and its development is important. Therefore the appearance of separate events trains the intellect. Otherwise full use of the intuitions would be relied upon and the intellect would not develop, for the intellect is an important feature in the further specialization of individual consciousness and identity.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第197节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "197", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0140", "zh": "直觉必须与理性并用，在解释你们的资料时，理性的用处是可以让自我了解资料内容。直觉很接近人类的根源，若想获得梦实相的相关讯息，得要透过直觉。", "en": "The intuitions must go hand in hand with the intellect. The intellect is useful in interpreting your data in terms that the ego can understand. The intuitions come close to mankinds source, and it is through the intuitions that information pertaining to the dream reality will come.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第174节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "174", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0437", "zh": "其一相信意识心和理性拥有一切答案，但对这学派而言，这是指意识心主要是分析作用，而他们仅透过理性就找到了所有答案。另一派相信答案是在情感和情绪中。但是两者皆错。理性和情感一同造成你的存在。他们最大的错误就是相信知觉最重要的作用必须是分析性的，而非对“直觉的心及知识”了解和消化。", "en": "One believes that the conscious mind and the intellect have all the answers, but to this school this means that the conscious mind is analytical above all, and that it can find all the answers through reason alone. The other school believes that the answers are in feelings and emotion. Both are wrong. Intellect and feeling together make up your existence, but the fallacy is particularly in the belief that the aware mind must be analytical above all, as opposed to, for example, the understanding or assimilation of intuitive psychic knowledge.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第638节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "638", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0577", "zh": "有些人在理智上极为熟练，他们的推理能力是无庸置疑的；然而，就你们的评估而言，你却看不见他们相当缺乏，比如说，情感或灵性的发展。当然，这种人并不认为是智障。我会一直谈到在直觉与推理能力之间的平衡，而我希望引领你们朝向那些能力的结合。因为它们能携手带来在你们世界里必然会显得像是全新的一种能力，结合了两者的最佳因子，但却是以这样一种方式，使得两者都被不可计量的加强了。", "en": "There are people who are highly intellectually proficient, whose reasoning abilities are undisputed, and yet their considerable lack of, say, emotional or spiritual development remains largely invisible as far as your assessments are concerned. Such people are not considered retarded, of course. I will always be speaking about a balance between intuitional and reasoning abilities and, I hope, [be] leading you toward a wedding of those abilities, for together they can bring about what would certainly appear in your world to be one completely new faculty, combining the very best elements of each, but in such a fashion that both were immeasurably enhanced.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第914节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "914", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0498", "zh": "不过，除此之外，它还包含了你们也许可称为提示的东西，那会自动打开你们自己觉察的更大层面，因而把对你也存在其中的“未知的实相”之一些认识带入你有意识的生活。那主题本身就引诱出你的想象力。然后，那直觉性的能力会光照知性，使得它学会以一种比它以前所用的更广大，更令人兴奋，并且具生产力的方式去问问题。", "en": "Besides this, however, it contains what you may call cues that automatically open up greater levels of your own awareness, and hence bring into your conscious life some recognition of the unknown reality in which you also have your being. The subject matter itself entices your imagination. That intuitive faculty will then illuminate the intellect so that it learns to question in a broader, more exciting and productive manner than perhaps it did before.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第743节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "743", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0609", "zh": "举例来说，早期人类自发地扮演着其它动物的角色。他扮演一株树、一弯溪流、一块岩石。演戏变成了一种教学方法——一种传递信息的方法。（停顿很久。）人类永远拥有他所需的所有知识。要务在使它能具体的为人所得。像鲁柏这类人，以许多方式转译内在的知识——借由演出它，借由唱歌或跳舞，借由在山洞的墙壁上画出影像。将这种信息实际的利用，则是知性的工作，因而直觉与知性能携手合作。（停顿良久。）那时，人类以一种更直接的方式处理自发的知晓。", "en": "Early man, for example, spontaneously played at acting out the part of other animals. He took the part of a tree, a brook, a rock. Acting became a teaching method — a way of passing on information. (Long pause.) Man always possessed all of the knowledge he needed. The task was to make it physically available. People like Ruburt translated inner knowledge in many ways — through acting it out, through singing or dancing, through drawing images on cave walls. It was the intellect’s job to put such information to practical use, and thus the intuitions and the intellect worked hand in hand. (Long pause.) Man dealt then with spontaneous knowing in a more direct fashion.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第17节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "17", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0608", "zh": "可是，在那些时代，人更认同他直觉性的自己及他的想象力，而这些，在某个程度，在那时比在现在，更指挥了他的知性用在何方。", "en": "In those times, however, man identified more with his intuitive self, and with his imagination, and these to some extent more than now, directed the uses to which he put his intellect.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第15节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "15", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0544", "zh": "在另一方面你们的直觉却追随着一种不同的组织，你们的想象力也一样——牵涉到将事件带到统一之中，那常常是不为因果的限制所局限的。那么，以那种说法，“架构二”与联想打交道，因此在它内，物质世界的可认知事件可以通过无数的方式放在一起，然后再按照你心理上形成的那些联想所给它们的指示，出现在你的私人经验里。", "en": "On the other hand your intuitions follow a different kind of organization, as does your imagination — one involved with associations, an organization that unifies diverse elements and brings even known events together in a kind of unity that is often innocent of the limitations dictated by cause and effect. In those terms, then, Framework 2 deals with associations, so that within it the recognizable events of the physical world can be put together in an infinite number of ways, after which they appear in your private experience according to directions you have given them through those associations that you form mentally.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第825节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "825", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "它从哪儿来：一条叫「内在感官」的接收通道", "note": "赛斯把直觉定位成接收，不是一种天赋。他说意念特质先被内在感官接收到，有时候以直觉的方式被接收，然后灵光乍现于意识心（第31节）；他把第六种内在感官直接比作内我的直觉（第39节）；他又说情感是内在感官的外在延伸，所以你要靠直觉、靠情感路径的旅行才联络得上内我（第49节）。这条通道通向的那一层，是他整门哲学的支点：你比你的意识心大得多，而你不承认的那个自己恰好是你最重要的部分——它保证你在自己创造的物质宇宙里生存，是你与内在实相的连结部分，里面装着你迫切需要的知识、直觉与记忆（第23节）。《个人实相的本质》第622节他骂得直接：要停止相信内我是一座塞满令人厌恶的被压抑情绪的地牢——它确实有些被压抑的情绪，但也包含伟大的直觉、知识和你所有问题的答案。为什么家人之间、自己内部会有那种说不清的知？第227节给的答案是：对自己的任何一部分而言，都有一份非专门化、极其一般而直觉的知识，知道其他部分所经验的本质。第235节推得更远：自己还有别的有意识的部分，自我一点都不熟，但潜意识对它们有直觉的知识。第28节留了一个很好用的图像——鲁柏的直觉是一道门户，能让那个原本固执又专制的意识自我松下来。", "src": "《早期课》第1册第23、31、39、49、28节；第5册第227、235节；《个人实相的本质》第622节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 23 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 31 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 39 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 49 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 28 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 227 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 235 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 622 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0025", "zh": "一旦创建了这个伪装模式，智力对它的操控就非常重要。你创建了你的世界，你的智力就应该帮你应对你创建了的一切。智力还具有我在以后的日子要列举的其他重要功能。不过，我再说几次也不为多：你比你的意识心还大，大多了，你不承认的那个自己恰好就是自己最重要的部分，它不仅保证了你自己在已经创造的物质宇宙中的生存，而且也是你与内在实相的自己的连结部分。说到底，这就是唯一的基本实相，也持续让你有能力创造这些伪装模式，而且，如果你们终究要了解你们自己，如果人类终究要完全进化，那它也包含你们迫切需要的知识、直觉和记忆。", "en": "The intellect is extremely important in the manipulation of camouflage patterns once they are created. You have made your world, and your intellect should help you deal with what you have created. It has other vital functions which I shall enumerate at a later date. However, I cannot say this too often: You are more than your conscious mind, much more, and the self which you do not admit happens to be the portion of yourself which not only insures your own survival in the physical universe which it has made, but which is also the connective portion of yourself with inner reality. Which is, when all is said and done, the only basic reality; and which also continually enables you to create these camouflage patterns, and which contains knowledge and intuitions and memories which you need in a most desperate manner if you are ever to understand yourselves, and if the race of mankind is ever to evolve to its fullest.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第23节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "23", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0030", "zh": "这些模式按照一定的法则而演化。它们只是反映其背后的意念而已，而你必须认识到，这些意念源自不同的源头。它们起源于潜意识，这是事实，但是在这之前，意念特质（idea quality）会被内在感官接收到。有时候，意念特质会以直觉的方式被接收到，灵光乍现于意识心。意识自我（conscious ego）是伪装模式的主要操纵者，也是明显的执行者。生命力是形成伪装模式的实际材料，它存在着，而且被你们的人格无意识地运用。", "en": "The patterns evolve according to certain laws. They merely reflect the ideas behind them, and these ideas you must realize originate from different sources. They originate in the subconscious, it is true, but before this an idea quality is received by the inner senses. Sometimes this idea quality is received as intuition, where it sparks into the conscious mind. But the conscious ego is the primary manipulator of camouflage patterns and the obvious mover. The actual material from which camouflage patterns are formed is the vitality which exists and which is unconsciously used by your personalities.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第31节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "31", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0041", "zh": "还有一些其他的东西，我想简短提一下。那就是，我们曾简单谈过的第六种感官，它在某些方面可以连结到内我的直觉。这一部分我们下一节课也会讨论。", "en": "There is something else I wanted to mention briefly. It is that the sixth inner sense, of which we have spoken briefly, can be likened in some respects to the instincts of the inner self. This will be discussed also at our next session.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第39节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "39", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0050", "zh": "我也解释了能量如何转化和改变，如何调整自己适应任何一个层面特定的伪装模式。现在，在这些测验中，你将会接近内我。那么，其结果会是在物质上有其效力。情感是内在感官的外在延伸，于是通过直觉和旅行，情感路径的旅行，你将会连络上内我，因而能够用同样的方式带回这个讯息。", "en": "I have also explained how energy is transformed, and changes, adapting itself to the particular camouflage pattern of any given plane. Now in these tests you will reach the inner self. The results will be, then, valid in physical terms. The emotions are the outer extensions of the inner senses, and it is therefore through the intuitions and traveling, the traveling of the pathways of the emotions, that you will come in contact with the inner self, and therefore be able to carry back this information in the same manner.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第49节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "49", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0162", "zh": "在一个家庭里，对其中成员的经验是有一个广泛的了解，但这些是二手的，除了那些以家庭为单位所共享的经验外。这是重要的一点，因为就自己的任何部分而言，这里有一个非专门化的、非常一般和直觉的知识在自己的任何部分，是关于自己的其他部分所感受到的经验本质。", "en": "There is within the family a general realization of the experiences of its members, but these are second-handed, except for those experiences which the family shares as a unit. This is an important point, for there is an unspecialized, extremely generalized and intuitional knowledge on the part of any portion of the self, as to the nature of experience as felt by the other portions of the self.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第227节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "227", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0169", "zh": "不过，这个自己有其他自己意识的部分，这些是自我一点都不熟悉的，但对此潜意识有着直觉的知识。这个自己的这些自己意识部分存在于不同的实相系统。在我们开始殷斯翠姆博士资料之前，让我提醒你，无论如何，这里有一个全我，由这些不同自己意识的自己们所组成，因此自己的一部分的确意识到那个存在着去形成整个心理完形的整体。", "en": "There are other self-conscious portions of the self however, with which the ego is not at all familiar, but of which the subconscious has intuitive knowledge. These self-conscious portions of the self exist in different reality systems. Before we go into our Dr. Instream material, let me remind you however that there is a whole self, composed of these various self-conscious selves, and that a portion of the self is indeed aware of the unity that exists to form the whole psychological gestalt.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第235节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "235", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0431", "zh": "在这种例子里，悲叹地说“我是想了解自己，却又怕我不会喜欢自己发现的东西”是没有用的。你自己本身必须改变信念。你必须不再相信，“内我”是个充满了令人厌恶、被压抑情绪的地牢。它的确藏有一些被压抑的情绪，但也包含了伟大的直觉、知识，以及你所有问题的答案。", "en": "It does no good in such a case to bemoan the situation and say, “I want to understand myself but I’m frightened that I will not like what I find.” You yourself must change your beliefs. You must stop believing that the inner self is a dungeon of unsavory repressed emotion. It does contain some repressed emotion. It also contains great intuition, knowledge, and the answers to all of your questions.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第622节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "622", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0028", "zh": "有一两次他寻找征兆，这简直是不健康的反应。一来，鲁柏的自我极其强大。鲁柏的直觉是个门户，可以放松原本固执又专制的意识自我。然而，他的直觉特性并不轻浮，人格也已经整合。他对这件事没有恐惧。", "en": "Once or twice he looked for signs, and this is hardly a healthy reaction. For one thing, Ruburt's ego is extremely strong. Ruburt’s intuition is the gateway that relaxes an otherwise stubborn and domineering conscious ego. The intuitive qualities however are not frivolous, and the personality is integrated. Have no fear of this.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第28节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "28", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "为什么接不到：不是没有，是自我不肯信", "note": "赛斯说直觉从不缺席，缺席的是自我肯不肯接。第181节讲得最清楚：某些训练把自我逼得太僵、限制了它对其他实相的感知，直觉的经验就装不进它看到的那套实相架构，于是被退回——不是没收到，是格式不对。第161节他说这个人格的自我不信任自己的内在组织，非站远一点盯着它们不可，可它也切不干净，因为直觉仍然会说话；第88节说得更重：他的自我本来有变成他那直觉自己的僵化监狱的危险。约瑟是反面教材——他一直都有纪律，害怕信任自己的直觉，早年的生命情境把这个恐惧养大（第102节）。第314节赛斯点破了那些自律动作的真实身份：它们本来就是拿来抑制冲动或直觉行为的检查装置，而鲁柏对自己起疑的那些特质，恰恰是让这些课与他的发展成为可能的那些特质。第392节他把失眠解释成自我最后的挣扎：他的自我确实不信任直觉的自己，还一直嫉妒它。《个人实相的本质》第615节他把这场内在战争直接撤销：富有直觉力的自己和意识心之间原本无战事，看起来有，只因为你不肯面对意识心为你打开的全部资料。《灵魂永生》第514节还有一类很日常的自我取消：你会把十分合法的直觉感知合理化掉——房间突然对你显得又小又挤，你认定那是自己的想象，而房间并没有变。另一条线更客气，同样是拦路石，就是文化给直觉打的分数。《心灵的本质》第772节：理性与理智被认作男性特质、是文明与科学的骨架，直觉与冲动则被认作反复无常、不可靠、该被控制的。《个人与群体事件的本质》第853节说你们的科学家大体是知性取向的，相信理性超乎直觉之上，还理所当然地把两者当成对立项；第857节他给了一个反转的例子——那个忽然厌了科学知识之限制的科学家，把全部热忱交给他以为的反面即纯粹直觉知识，结果他阻挡理性，像先前阻挡直觉一样狂热。《梦、进化与价值完成》第914节他说你们社会把推理能力视为与直觉能力相反，于是人对一个人是怎么样或应该怎么样的概念里，大半忽略了情感成就与情感了解。《个人实相的本质》第653节记一笔道德账：那种态度让休息不被赞成、梦可疑、白日梦带上了道德意味，积极的运动算好，消极的直觉活动算坏。《神奇之道》第2节他借一个梦说：理性世界的观点并不代表安全堡垒，反而是完整利用知性与直觉的障碍。至于鲁柏自己：离开教会的架构之后，他就紧抓着心智来对抗他的直觉——没有能容纳那种经验的框架，成长中的孩子只好把它压下去，神秘经验只能透过诗或艺术被接受，他连一些婴儿也连同洗澡水泼掉了（《未知的实相》卷一第679节）。", "src": "《早期课》第3册第88、102节；第4册第161、181节；第7册第314节；第8册第392节；《灵魂永生》第514节；《个人实相的本质》第615、653节；《未知的实相》卷一第679节；《心灵的本质》第772节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第853、857节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第914节；《神奇之道》第2节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 88 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 102 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 161 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 181 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 314 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 392 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 514 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 615 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 653 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 679 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 772 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 853 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 857 节"}, {"n": 14, "id": null, "label": "第 914 节"}, {"n": 15, "id": null, "label": "第 2 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "自我把直觉当威胁", "note": "赛斯讲的个人层面：僵化、恐惧、嫉妒，全是自我在守门。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0142", "zh": "许多情况下，自我本身无法直接经验某些直觉和心理经验，但在理性的基础上，自我所能觉知的范围内，就可以经验到这些直觉和心理经验。如果某些训练迫使自我变得太过僵化，也会限制它感知其他实相，此时自我就无法接收到直觉，因为这个直觉经验并不符合自我看到的实相架构。", "en": "The ego itself in many instances cannot experience directly certain intuitions and psychological experiences, but it can experience them insofar as it can be aware of them on an intellectual basis. When training forces the ego to become too rigid, and to limit its perception of other realities, then the intuitions will not be accepted by the ego because intuitional experience will not fit into the framework of reality as the ego sees it.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第181节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "181", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0130", "zh": "这个人格的自我并不信任自己的内在组织，自我必须设法远离它们、监视它们，不相信它们对自我的态度得当。由于自我必须将自己与内我切割开来，但这完全不可能，因为直觉仍然会说话，而且因为自我害怕自己会非常孤独，于是就处在目前的情境中。", "en": "The ego of the personality does not trust its own inner organisms. It must attempt to stand apart from them, and keep an eye on them. The ego does not believe that they are treating it right. The ego is therefore in its present circumstances because it fears itself so solitary, since it has to a large degree cut itself off from its inner self; yet not entirely, for the intuitive still speaks.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第161节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "161", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0082", "zh": "他的自我本来会置身很大的风险之中，变成他那直觉自己的一个僵化的监狱，因为他非得采用必要的防卫机制，抵御他母亲人格中最难应付和最具威胁性的面向不可。", "en": "His ego would have been in great danger of becoming a rigid prison for his intuitive self, because of the necessary defensive mechanisms it had to adopt against the most difficult and threatening aspects of his mother's personality.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第88节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "88", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0108", "zh": "你，约瑟，一直都有纪律。你害怕信任你的直觉，你早年的生命情境助长了这个恐惧。但你现在已经学会信任你自己，并据以扩展了。你现在是自由的，你也会在你的绘画和你生命中的其他面向继续增长你的能力。", "en": "You, Joseph, had the discipline always. You were afraid to trust your intuitions, and the circumstances of your early life encouraged this fear. But you have now learned to trust yourself and have expanded accordingly. You are now free, and you will continue to expand your abilities, in your painting and other aspects of your life.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第102节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "102", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0235", "zh": "我们要把这一点说清楚，因为他的自我实际上并不信任直觉的自己，而且一直嫉妒它。然而，因为一直有心灵扩展的现象，所以最近就有所斩获，而近来的睡眠问题，起因于自我的爆发、最后的挣扎；是一种相当微弱的攻击。", "en": "Now we shall put this plainly, for his ego has indeed distrusted his intuitional self, and has been jealous of it. There has been a spiritual expansion occurring however that is responsible for these recent gains, and the late difficulty in sleeping has been the result of a flare up, a last struggle, on the part of the ego; a rather weak offensive.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第392节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "392", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0194", "zh": "这些本来就是在抑制冲动或直觉的行为。所以他认为他的言行一定要慎重、合理、安静又自律；而且为了看到他的确是，他让身体的动作尽其所能减慢速度。现在，这是问题的核心，他不让我早一点说出来。他应该，而且说真的，也必须是他自己。他对他自己起了疑心的那些特质，就是让我们的课以及他的发展成为可能的那些特质。", "en": "These were meant as checks against impulsive or intuitive behavior. He must then behave, he thought, in a measured, reasoned, quiet, calm and disciplined way: and to see that he did, he slowed down the motions the body could make. Now, this is the heart of the matter, and he would not let me give it earlier. He should, and indeed, must, be himself. Those qualities of his of which he became suspicious are those that made our sessions and his development possible.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第314节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "314", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0423", "zh": "在富有直觉力的自己和意识心之间，原本无战事。表面上看来这件事存在的原因，好像是你拒绝去面对“意识心”为你开放的全部资枓。（停顿。） 这样做，有时候似乎较易逃避自省之后必须常常面临的自我凋整。但是，逃避的结果却会使你收集许多二手货的信念。这些信念中有些是相互矛盾的，由于这种矛盾，你对身体与内我发出的讯号也不顺畅、不清晰了，变成互相抵触的纷乱杂讯。", "en": "There is no battle between the intuitive self and the conscious mind. There only seems to be when the individual refuses to face all the information that is available in his conscious mind. (Pause.) Sometimes it seems easier to avoid the frequent readjustments in behavior that self-examination requires. In such cases an individual collects many secondhand beliefs. Some contradict each other; the signals given to the body and to the inner self are not smoothly flowing or clear-cut, but a muddied jumble of counter-directions.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第615节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "615", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0365", "zh": "如我告诉你们的，我的环境不断在变化，但你们自己的也是如此。在这种时候你把十分合法的直觉性感知加以合理化而不顾。好比说，如果一个房间对你突然显得又小又挤，你更会认定这种尺寸的改变是出自于自己的想象，而房间并没变，不管你的感觉如何。", "en": "My environment, as I told you, changes constantly, but then, so does your own. You rationalize away quite legitimate intuitive perception at such times. For example, if a room suddenly appears small and cramped to you, you take it for granted that this change of dimension is imaginative, and that the room has not changed regardless of your feelings.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第514节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "514", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "一套教出来的偏见", "note": "社会与专业给的差评：直觉＝女性、非理性、不可靠，于是被管起来。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0517", "zh": "一般而言，理性与理智于是被认作是男性特质（Generally, reason and intellect are then considered male qualities），以及是文明、科学和组织化的世界之构架。直觉与冲动则被认作是反复无常的、不可靠的、女性的，而该被控制。世界因为自发性而存在。文明因为人们想要在一起的冲动而开始，它自发的生长而进入秩序。你只看到许多过程的外表，因为你们客观化的观点不允许你认同更多内容的显示。在你看来，似乎所有的系统在某个时候都崩溃——变得较无秩序或流入混乱之中。", "en": "Generally, reason and intellect are then considered male qualities, and the frameworks for civilization, science, and an organized world. The intuitions and the impulses are considered erratic, untrustworthy, feminine, and to be controlled. The world exists because of spontaneous order. Civilization began because of the impulse of people to be together. It grew spontaneously and came into order. You only see the outside of many processes because your objectified viewpoint does not allow you the identification that would show you more. It seems to you then that all systems sometime break down — become less orderly or fall into chaos.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第772节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "772", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0553", "zh": "一般而言，你们的科学家是知性取向的，相信理性超乎直觉之上，而理所当然的把那些特质视为是对立的。他们无法想象（停顿）生命“最初的”创造性源头，因为，以他们的说法，那会提醒他们创造力之女性基础。", "en": "Your scientists are, generally now, intellectually oriented, believing in reason above the intuitions, taking it for granted that those qualities are opposites. They cannot imagine (pause) life’s “initial” creative source, for in their terms it would remind them of creativity’s feminine basis.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第853节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "853", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0559", "zh": "民主的理念表现了一个高度理想主义之存在——它要求政治与社会组织到某个程度能有效将那些理想付诸实现（强调的）。当那些组织失败了，而在理想主义与被实现的善之间的鸿沟变得太大时，那么这种情况就会使一些理想主义者变成狂热份子。（停顿良久）那些非常严格的尊崇科学或宗教指令的人，可以在一瞬间就改变立场，科学家开始玩起了通灵术，而当他突然的对科学知识的限制感到厌恶时，他就会把他所有的热忱给了他认为的反面或直觉性的知识，但是如此做时，他阻挡了他的理性，就像他先前阻档他的直觉一样的狂热。相信达尔文定律及生存竞争，把不公平甚至偷窃以“适者生存”的概念来合理化的那些商人——突然他变成了基督教的基本教义派分子，那么，他也许想借由把他聚集的财富施舍掉，以试图获得力量感，这全都是一种纠缠不清的企图，想在一个实际的世界里表达一种自然的理想主义。", "en": "The idea [of democracy] expresses the existence of a high idealism — one that demands political and social organizations that are effective to some degree in providing some practical expression of those ideals (emphatically). When those organizations fail and a gulf between idealism and actualized good becomes too great, then such conditions help turn some idealists into fanatics. (Long pause.) Those who follow with great strictness the dictates of either science or religion can switch sides in a moment. The scientist begins tipping tables or whatever, and suddenly disgusted by the limits of scientific knowledge, he turns all of his dedication to what he thinks of as its opposite, or pure intuitive knowledge. Thus, he blocks his reason as fanatically as earlier he blocked his intuitions. The businessman who believed in Darwinian principles and the fight for survival, who justified injustice and perhaps thievery to his ideal of surviving in a competitive world — he suddenly turns into a fundamentalist in religious terms, trying to gain his sense of power now, perhaps, by giving away the wealth he has amassed, all in a tangled attempt to express a natural idealism in a practical world.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第857节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "857", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0578", "zh": "且说，就人类而言，所有的变奏都是必要的。就像是在一个例子里人类的一员——为他自己，但也为了全体——决定在一个特定区域专门化，可说是孤立某些能力，而以最大的固执及聪明展现它们，同时几乎完全忽略某些其他的领域。可是在你们的社会里，推理心的能力被认为是与直觉能力相反的，所以，你们对于一个人是怎么样或应该怎么样的概念，大半忽略了情感成就及情感了解。", "en": "Now as far as the species is concerned, all variations are necessary—and it is as if (underlined) in one instance a member of the species—for its own reasons, but also on behalf of the whole—decides to specialize in one particular area, to isolate certain abilities, so to speak, and display them with the greatest tenacity and brilliance, while nearly completely ignoring certain other areas. In your society, however, the capacities of the reasoning mind have been considered in opposition to the intuitive abilities, so that your ideas of what a person is or should be largely ignore the idea of emotional achievement, emotional understanding.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第914节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "914", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0445", "zh": "这种想法本身带来了一个全面性的态度，而对休息不表赞同，并且对梦也没什么好感。白日梦与其至意识轻微的改变，也是一种道德上的缺失。这种意念以无数的方式，在你们的社会上以及那些善恶价值并不明显的领域反映出来。然而积极的运动被认为是好的，却常常被拿来与消极的直觉活动对比，而被认为后者是坏的。", "en": "This kind of thinking by itself brings about an overall attitude in which rest is frowned upon, and dreams are considered suspect. Daydreaming and even mild alterations of consciousness take on moral connotations. Such ideas are mirrored in your society in innumerable fashions, and in areas in which values of good and evil are not apparent. Active sports are considered good, however, but often contrasted to passive intuitive activities which are then seen as bad.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第653节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "653", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0588", "zh": "不论你有没有看到那段（出现在艾尔默拉报纸上的）报导，那梦都达到了它的目的。事实上，不论你记得它与否，那梦都达到了目的，不过你却是记得的。你记得它，因为你想将你自己知道的例子带入你有意识的范围。形成那梦的你的那个部分知道那污染，但也知道那补偿金、报上的报导，及你看晚报的习惯。所有那一切涉及了自然的、神奇的意念之心理动态。它显示给你看，理性世界的法则是充满了漏洞的。它显示给你看，理性世界的观点并不代表安全堡垒，反之，却是完整利用知性和直觉的障碍。", "en": "The dream made its point, whether or not you read the article that later appeared (in the Elmira paper). The dream made its point, in fact, whether or not you remembered it, though you did. You remembered it because you wanted to bring into your conscious range instances of your own greater knowing. The portion of you that formed the dream knew of the pollution; but also knew of the award, the newspaper article, and of your habit of reading the evening’s paper. All of that involves a psychological motion of natural, magical import. It shows you that the rules of the rational world are filled with holes. It shows you that the rational world’s views do not represent the bulwarks of safety, but are instead barriers to the full use of the intellect, and of the intuitions.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第2节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "2", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0462", "zh": "那看起来沉着的孩子在某些方面其独断不屈并不比鲁柏差。但离开了教会架构之后，鲁柏就紧抓着心智来对抗他的直觉。在这照片里的孩子确信基督的雕像移动了，然而，没有一个架构去容纳那种经验，这成长中的孩子只好将之压抑下来。神秘经验变得只可透过诗或书而被接受，在那儿它被接受为具创造性的，却没有真实到会给他麻烦，或颠覆了那个“新的”架构。新的架构把这种迷信的无稽丢在一边，心智被控制住了，而艺术变成神秘经验之可被接受的转译，而且是那个经验与自己之间的一个缓冲。他这种作法有点因噎废食了。", "en": "The placid-looking child (in the photo) was as dogmatic and unyielding in some respects as Ruburt has ever been. Yet leaving the church framework, Ruburt fastened upon the mind as opposed to the intuitions. The child here was convinced that statues of Christ moved. Without a framework to contain that kind of experience, the growing girl began to squash it. Mystical experience became acceptable only through poetry or art, where it was accepted as creative, but not real enough to get him into trouble, or to upset the “new” framework. The new framework threw aside such superstitious nonsense. The mind would be harnessed, and art became the acceptable translator of mystical experience, and a cushion between that experience and the self. He threw some of the baby out with the bathwater.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第679节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "679", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "怎么让它工作：给自由，别逼迫", "note": "赛斯给的方法里几乎没有「努力」这一项，全是叫你别再挡路。第186节他连着讲了三步：意识心与自我必须短暂退离，好让直觉的自己获得自由；他应该知道灵感不是来自自我——这事他头脑上很清楚，却偏要把自我当皮鞭来鞭策自己加快脚步；只要他不再一直逼迫直觉的本性就范，那本性会很乐意回应，而且不费吹灰之力；心理时间的实验也该暂停，意识心一转移注意力，直觉就开始尽它的本分。第205节教的是姿势：不要想我们，要感觉我们；自我暗示有用，因为它把你放进心智较直觉的那个模式。第94节说的是焦点：放下自我中心的栅栏，光是焦点的改变就有利于直觉的领悟。第37节给了一个几乎像练习的说法：凭直觉往外去接触那个观念，别害怕也别拒绝随之而来的身体感觉，练习之后你会发现自己能变成那个观念，站在里面往外看，而不是往里面看。第440节他给了反例：只要你坚持要生命走某些意识中预先定好的路、专注在你所没有的东西上，就找不到生命的目的与意义，那会耗尽你的能量、迟钝你的直觉。对约瑟与鲁柏这对组合，他的处方一直是反着开的：你已经够自律了，该给直觉更大的自由（第84节）；你的自律要跟着直觉走（第84节）；而他必须允许自己的直觉自己展现出来（第58节）。第283节讲到了转折点：外在自我感应到那些通常对它关着门的实相，想到「还有更多，但是我无法跟过去」——就在这一刻，内在自我可能突然打开，直觉的泉源冲到表面，因为它已经先被叫醒，能一面接住这些实相、一面照常履行日常职责；接着它再也不怕直觉的资料，不再跟内在感官打仗，也不再担心自己在直觉的洪流里活不活得下来。第308节把纪律加了回来：接收的范围一旦打开就不再对你完全封闭，而一个自律但直觉的自我随之变成必要——新经验要被管住，自我因此更有必要而不是更没必要；把它晾到一边，它会武装起来反抗，那可能非常危险。第74节他把两样合在一起开成作息：完全的直觉加上有纪律的控制，再配上包含沉思与暂时放慢身体过程的日常安排，他因此活得更久，作品也更有深度。《神奇之道》第8节他把这件事写成身份问题：要记住你自己的自然人，就是别只与知性认同，而要把身份的范围放大，让直觉、感受、梦与神奇的希望被当作「个人性」的重要特性，而不是附属物。最后是他自己下的钩子：他说这本书每一章都刻意这样写，好让呈现的观念发动读者自己的直觉，打开做梦与醒时状态之间的通路（《心灵的本质》第790节）；《灵魂永生》第511节他说希望这书释出每一位读者内在那个极为直觉的自己，把对你最有用的个别洞见带到意识前面；《健康之道》第10节他说他在加快加强那些让你身心平安、因而便利你使用自己直觉能力的坐标。最早的一句鼓励在《早期课》第1册第17节：相信你的直觉，你的确具有直觉，完全没有必要害怕它们。", "src": "《早期课》第1册第17、37节；第2册第58、74、84节；第3册第94节；第4册第186节；第5册第205节；第7册第283、308节；第9册第440节；《灵魂永生》第511节；《心灵的本质》第790节；《神奇之道》第8节；《健康之道》第10节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 17 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 37 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 74 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 84 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 94 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 186 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 205 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 283 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 308 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 440 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 511 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 790 节"}, {"n": 14, "id": null, "label": "第 8 节"}, {"n": 15, "id": null, "label": "第 10 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "把自我暂时挪开", "note": "核心动作是松开，不是加力。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0144", "zh": "意识心、自我，一定要短暂退离，好让直觉的自己获得自由。他应该知道，灵感不是来自于自我。他的头脑对这一点很清楚，但在这种状况下，他坚持要把自我当成皮鞭，用来鞭策自己加快脚步。过去他比较能知觉到这一方面。", "en": "The conscious mind, the ego, must be momentarily diverted, so that the intuitive self is allowed freedom. He should know that inspiration does not come from the ego. He knows this intellectually, but upon this occasion he insists in using his ego as a whip to force speed. In the past he was more sensible in this respect.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第186节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "186", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0145", "zh": "如果他将用来放松或从事其他休闲的时间，视为一种浪费，而且讨厌这些时刻，那可就不行。只要他不再一直逼迫直觉的本性就范，那么直接的本性会很乐于回应，而且不费吹灰之力。", "en": "It will not do if he resents the time he thinks is lost in relaxation or other pursuits. His intuitive nature will respond easily and enthusiastically when he stops trying to beat it into submission.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第186节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "186", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0146", "zh": "心理时间的实验也该暂停。如果意识心能转移注意力，直觉能力就会尽其本分开始运作了。约瑟，你教他自律的这一部分做得很好，不过因为他做事从来就不会半途而废，所以有时候学东西会过度认真。这里还有一个重点：你自己的工作节奏跟他不一样。", "en": "The psychological-time experiments should also be suspended. When the conscious mind is so diverted the intuitions can do their work. You did well Joseph, teaching him discipline, but as he never goes halfway, so sometimes he learns his lessons too well. One point here also: you pace yourselves differently in your work.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第186节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "186", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0152", "zh": "这很难诉诸语言。不要想到我们，要感觉我们，让我们看看可以怎么做。如果可能，自我暗示是最有利的，那会把你放在心智的一个较直觉的模式下。把你的情感转向我们，那我想我们就能接收到你的物件。", "en": "This is difficult to put into words. Feel toward us rather than think at us, and let us see how we do. Self-suggestion may be most beneficial when possible, when used to put you in this more intuitive frame of mind. Turn your emotions towards us, and I think we’ll be able to pick up your objects.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第205节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "205", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0098", "zh": "解离状态是必要的，放下自我中心的栅栏（barriers），才能明了和辨别内在的象征。光是焦点的改变就有助于直觉的领悟，如此一来潜意识各区才能够更加容易串联起来。", "en": "A state of dissociation is necessary, a letting down of egotistical barriers in order that inner symbolisms can be appreciated and distinguished. The change of focus alone will aid in intuitional enlightenment, and association can then rise more easily through the subconscious areas.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第94节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "94", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0037", "zh": "凭直觉往外接触观念，不要害怕或拒绝身体的感觉。透过练习，程度非常有限，但你会发现你可以变成这个观念。你将在观念里面，往外看，而不是往内看。这是思想（thought）。", "en": "Reach out to the idea intuitively. Do not be afraid of or reject unfamiliar bodily sensations. With practice, and to a very limited degree, you will find that you can become the idea. You will be inside the idea, looking out, not looking in. This is thought.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第37节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "37", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0284", "zh": "只要你坚持要生命走某些意识中预先定好的路，只要你专注于你所没有的东西，你就不会发现你生命的目的与意义。这会耗尽你的能量，迟钝你的直觉。你的确被结婚的念头和对男人的爱迷住了；但正如约瑟[Joseph]所说，这只是一个症状。", "en": "You will not discover the purpose and meaning of your life when you insist that it follow certain consciously predetermined roads, and while you concentrate upon what you do not have. This saps your energy and dulls your intuitions. You are indeed obsessed with the idea of marriage, and with male love, but as Joseph mentioned this is but a symptom.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第440节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "440", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "给它范围，也给它纪律", "note": "赛斯从不叫自我退场，他要的是「自律但直觉」的组合。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0078", "zh": "说真的，他有一种特别懒散的习惯，如果他的艺术天赋要开花结果，就必须克服这个习惯。还有你，亲爱的朋友，如果你能够给你的直觉更大的自由就好了，因为你已经够自律（self-discipline）了。", "en": "He is given, indeed, to a peculiar habit of sloth which he must conquer if his artistic abilities are to bear fruit. And you, dear friend, could do with giving your intuitions greater freedom, for you are already adequately blessed with self-discipline.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第84节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "84", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0054", "zh": "这些课很显然是这件事尚未发生的证明。但因为有你的帮助，他现在将会在自由之内找到纪律。然而，他必须允许自己的直觉自己展现出来。", "en": "These sessions are obviously proof that this has not yet occurred. But he will find now, because of your help, discipline within freedom. He must allow himself however the freedom for his intuitions to show themselves.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0080", "zh": "马克正在很慎重地考虑一件事。但是除非他能好好研究一下自己，否则他会付出惨痛的代价，了解到他想要做的那件事必须靠自律才能贯彻到底。你应该知道，你的自律是跟着直觉走的。如果你们不介意，我要说，鲁柏既不过分自律，也不过分凭直觉做事。", "en": "Mark is considering a commitment to an idea. Unless he studies himself most thoroughly, he must take great pains to see that the commitment is followed up by self-discipline. You should see to it that your self-discipline follows the dictates of intuition. If you will excuse the comment, Ruburt is either all self-discipline or all intuition.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第84节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "84", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0183", "zh": "外在自我感应到它通常不得其门而入的实相。它想：“还有更多，但是我无法跟过去。”这里，有了这个了悟之后，内在自我可能会突然开启。直觉泉源冲到表面，因为外在自我已经改变了，它能够接受这些实相，同时依然履行它平常的职责。", "en": "It senses realities usually closed to it. It thinks, “There is more, but beyond I cannot follow.” Here with this realization the inner ego may suddenly open. Intuitive springs rush to the surface, and because the outer ego has already been alerted, it is able to accept these realities while still performing its ordinary duties.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0184", "zh": "然后可以取得的知识首先是创造、直觉的知识，如果可能，外在自我就会翻译成理智层面的说法。但它再也不怕直觉资料。它再也不抗拒内在感官，也不再恐惧它自己在直觉洪流之中的存活。", "en": "The knowledge then available is first of all creative, intuitive knowledge which the outer ego may translate into intellectual terms when possible. But it is no longer fearful of intuitive data. It no longer fights the inner senses, nor does it fear for its own survival in the midst of intuitional onrushes.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第283节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "283", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0191", "zh": "障碍被铲除，一旦你习惯在更大的范围之内接收时，你在你的未来也能够这么做。这些范围一旦打开，往后就不会对你完全封闭。在你的未来，你会更容易在它们之内接收。 一个自律但直觉的自我接着会变成必要，好让这样的新经验可以得到有用的控制，按照你们的（划线）话来说。自我变得更有必要，你看，而不是更没必要，因为它必须学会在你们的系统之内用可以辨认的方式合成已有的经验。否则，自我要是被晾在一旁，它就会武装起来，进行反抗，所以可能非常危险。", "en": "Barriers are cut away, and once you become used to receiving within a larger range you will be able to do so in your future. These ranges, once opened up, then do not entirely close up to you. It becomes easier for you in your future to receive within them. A disciplined but intuitive ego then becomes a necessity in order that such new experience may be brought under useful control, in your (underlined) terms. The ego become more necessary you see, not less, for it must learn to synthesize the gained experience in recognizable terms within your system. Otherwise if the ego is pushed aside it will rise up in arms and in opposition, and can be highly dangerous.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第308节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "308", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0064", "zh": "运用完全的直觉和有纪律的控制，再加上包含冥想与短暂放松和放慢身体过程的日常作息，“意味着”他将因此而活得更长，而且他的作品也会比较有深度、比较有重大意义。", "en": "The use of full intuition with discipline and control, and a daily schedule that includes contemplation and a temporary relaxation and slowing down of bodily process, [means] he will live longer because of this, and his work will be deeper and of greater import.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第74节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "74", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0597", "zh": "纵然如此，男人和女人仍然借由重新发现更大意义的身分——那是接受直觉和感受、梦和神奇的希望为「个人性」之重要特性，而非附属物的一种身分感——而找到他们许多问题的答案。当我告诉你，要记住你自己的自然人时，那么我就是真的想要提醒你，别光只与你的知性认同，而应去扩大你身分的范围。然后自然而然地，那些其它的、往往被唾弃的特性，便开始毫不费力地将它们的丰富成就和活力，增加到你的生命里。", "en": "Despite all of that, men and women still find the solutions to many of their problems by rediscovering the larger sense of identity1 — a sense of identity that accepts the intuitions and the feelings, the dreams and the magic hopes as vital characteristics, not adjuncts, of personhood. When I tell you to remember your own natural persons, I do then want to remind you not to identify with your intellects alone, but to enlarge your scopes of identity. Automatically those other, often-shunted-aside characteristics begin to add their richness, fulfillment, and vitality to your lives effortlessly.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第6节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "6", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "赛斯自己怎么起手", "note": "他连写书的方式都是冲着读者的直觉去的。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0527", "zh": "我是个个人化能量的源头——而你们也是的。以你们的话来说，我曾度过许多生，但以另一种角度来看，我没有以肉身活过，而是把我的能量借贷给从我的实相升起，而却非我的那些生命。以同样的方式，你孕生自己的梦中影像——几乎未觉察你曾如此做，没意识到你被一种逃过了你注意力的心理实相提供了动力（In the same way you give birth to dream images of your own — hardly aware that you have done so, unconscious of the fact that you have provided impetus for a kind of psychological reality that quite escapes your notice.）。你所开始的梦的故事自己继续了下去。没有一个梦是死胎。这本书的每一章是以这样一种方式写出来，使得所呈现的概念将发动你们自己的直觉，而打开在你的做梦和醒时状态之间的通路。", "en": "I am a personified energy source — but so are you. I have had many lives, in your terms, yet in other terms I have not lived physically, but rather lent or loaned my energy to lives that rose from my reality but were not me. In the same way you give birth to dream images of your own — hardly aware that you have done so, unconscious of the fact that you have provided impetus for a kind of psychological reality that quite escapes your notice. The dream stories you begin continue on their own. No dream is stillborn. Each chapter of this book is written in such a way that the ideas presented will activate your own intuitions, and open pathways between your dreaming and waking states.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第790节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "790", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0362", "zh": "你们每一个人都曾有过其它的存在，虽然你们没有明白意识到，但这个知识是在你们内的。我希望这书会帮我的每一个读者释出他内在的那极为直觉性的自己，并把对你最有用的任何个别的洞见带到你意识的面前。", "en": "You have each lived other existences, and that knowledge is within you though you are not consciously aware of it. I hope that this book will serve to release the deeply intuitive self within each of my readers, and to bring to the foreground of consciousness whatever particular insights will serve you most.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第511节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "511", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0615", "zh": "再次的，我加快加强你们自己身心平安、而便利你们自己直觉能力利用的那些坐标。", "en": "Once again I quicken those coordinates that energize your own peace of body and mind, and facilitate the use of your own intuitive abilities.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0012", "zh": "相信你的直觉。你的确具有直觉。你完全没有必要害怕它们。你已经弥补了你的错误，约瑟。在你的发展当中有一度，我承认你的冲动并不是最好的。现在没有理由对它们一棒子打死。", "en": "Trust your intuitions. You do have them. There is absolutely no need for you to fear them. You have made up for your mistakes, Joseph. At one time in your development I admit your impulses were not of the best. That is no reason to club them to death now.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第17节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "17", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "它会不会说错？赛斯自己给了刻度", "note": "赛斯没有把直觉捧成不会错的雷达。第9节他说珍的直觉代表现在这个人对她整体存有的惊鸿一瞥，一般来得很强烈，可她和你一样不是在完全的存有层次上运作，所以你不能靠她的直觉去捕捉你可能犯的所有错误。第10节留下一段很有名的记录：直觉正确，但放错地方了——那个地方令她联想起另一生的另一个地方，那时狼来了，同样的季节、天色黑暗、树木繁茂，那一次还有一只狗陪着你们。第19节的措辞因此格外实用：当鲁柏对某个特定情况有强烈感觉，你该给这件事充分考虑，因为你通常、不是总是而是通常，可以相信他的直觉；同一节他还给了一套分工——你可以接受那份基本的直觉冲动，然后做自己的修改，比如更早离开那份工作，再按这个决定安排自己的计划；当你们两人都凭直觉被同一个行动建议吸引，那多半就该动。第210节是更难的一课：鲁柏在那里学着辨认「伴随着有效感知的不同主观感受」，并去区辨那些「建立在无效感知上的主观感受」——看错是可以被学会认出来的。反方向的账也照样在：《早期课》第9册第493节那个拐弯，比尔不敢开快车，却在霍斯黑兹凭一时直觉拐下钱伯斯路，最后在排水沟里找到了肯德尔的车。同一节他还批评另一种做法：课堂上你没有先做出原初的直觉判断，而是有意识地按国籍、年龄和你想到的条件去端详那些肖像——被动里有一个「被动而警觉」的点，你越过了它，就失去本可以看见的东西。第329节他承认直觉会跟想要的东西对打：你不会满意那个男人，而你在直觉上明了这一点；想得到他的那份痴迷，正好与内心明白自己不想要他的了悟成正比。《个人与群体事件的本质》第814节他甚至给医学打分：科学医学救命的时候，靠的是医生本身直觉的治愈性了解，或是病人被那份努力深深打动因而间接信服了自己的价值。《健康之道》第12节他说父母的直觉常会指向最合适的方向，前提是了解这种处境背后确实有个理由。《梦、进化与价值完成》第909节他把一手与二手摆平：任何仪器——不管多精密——给你的都是二手证据，而它们比思想、感受与直觉这些主观属性更扭曲实相的本质。《神奇之道》第8节：动物不读也不写书，但它们经由自己经验的范畴、经由直觉的知晓，直接阅读自然。最要紧的那句在《个人与群体事件的本质》第825节：到某个程度，你的直觉引介你一个事实——你在宇宙里有自己的位置，而那个宇宙本身对你有好感；直觉知道你独特而重要的角色，直觉知道宇宙偏向你这方；而你的推理只能处理肉体感知的结果，事实上是你不让它拿到那些重要资料，因为你教过它不信任心灵的能力。", "src": "《早期课》第1册第9、10、19节；第5册第210节；第7册第329节；第9册第493节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第814、825节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第909节；《神奇之道》第8节；《健康之道》第12节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 9 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 10 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 19 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 210 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 329 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 493 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 814 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 825 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 909 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 8 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 12 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "它会错，但错的方式有讲究", "note": "两句实话：通常可以信，但不是永远信；感觉可能是对的，放的地点却可能错。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0005", "zh": "珍的存有非常强壮。她的直觉代表现在她这个人对她整体存有的惊鸿一瞥。一般说来，这些直觉来得非常强烈。然而，她和你一样都不是在完全的存有层次上运作，所以你不能依赖她的直觉去捕捉所有你可能犯的错误。", "en": "Jane’s entity is an extremely strong one. Her intuition represents glimpses by her present person of her whole entity. As a rule these intuitions come through strongly. However, she is not operating at full entity level any more than you are, so you cannot rely upon her intuitions to catch all the mistakes that you may make.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第9节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "9", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0007", "zh": "直觉正确，但放错地方了。这地方令珍联想起另一生的另一个地方，那时狼来了。在同样的季节里，天色黑暗，并且树木繁茂。那一次也有一只狗与你们在一起。", "en": "Intuition correct but misplaced. Place reminiscent of another in another life, when the wolves came. Dark and wooded, same time of year. Also had dog with you that other time.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第10节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0021", "zh": "我并不是说鲁柏无论什么情况都应该要负责处理所有的个人事务。这种建议不是我的本意。我只是说，当鲁柏对一个特定的情况有某种强烈的感觉时，你就应该对这件事给予充分考虑，因为你通常，不是总是而是通常，可以相信他的直觉。", "en": "I did not mean that Ruburt should handle all your personal matters by any means. Such a suggestion was not my intention. I merely mean that when Ruburt feels strongly one way or another about a particular situation that you should give the matter deep thought and consideration, since you can usually, not always but usually, trust his intuitions.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第19节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "19", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0023", "zh": "有空我打算谈论一下鲁柏的特性，我真的会的。不过现在仍然是你，约瑟，我还会再关心你一阵子。事实是，鲁柏的直觉已经具有相当高的品质。而你的特有天赋也可以让鲁柏的很多想法有变化和理由。例如在很多情况下，你可以接受鲁柏基本的直觉冲动，然后做一些你自己的改变。比如，你可以更早离开那份工作，然后根据这个决定做出自己的计划。当你俩都凭着直觉被同一个行动建议吸引时，那么在大多数情况下，采取行动是明智的。因为你是如此——摇摆不定，这个字对不对？——做了练习之后， 我建议休息片刻。", "en": "I intend to go into Ruburt's peculiarities at my leisure, and I will. Nevertheless it is still you, Joseph, with whom I will be concerned for a while. The fact remains that Ruburt’s intuitions have been of fairly high quality. It is true that your particular talents can give variety and reason to many of Ruburt’s ideas. In many cases you could for example accept Ruburt’s basic intuitive impulse, and then make your own changes. For example you could have left your position at a much earlier time and then made your own plans accordingly. When you both are intuitively attracted to the same proposed move then in most cases it would be wise to make it. Because you are so—is the word wobbly?—after your exercises I suggest a short break.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第19节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "19", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0153", "zh": "不过在鲁柏的发展阶段，他对情绪刺激的结果起反应，他很直接地接收到，而这个行动是一个额外传递的能量。因为这个原因，他有时会很享受课程里有人拜访，因为他直觉地感觉到，他会因此而学会操纵和使用这些能力，也学会了伴随着有效感知的不同主观感受，和去区辨那些建立在无效感知上的主观感受。", "en": "At Ruburt’s stage of development however, he reacts as a result of emotional impetus, which is picked up rather directly, and which acts as additional energy in transmission. It is for this reason that he now and then does enjoy visitors to sessions, because he instinctively feels that he is thereby learning to manipulate and use these abilities oftentimes, and thereby learn the various subjective feelings that accompany valid perceptions, and to distinguish these from subjective feelings that turn out to be based upon invalid perceptions.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第210节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "210", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "它比理智更在场", "note": "论一手证据与判断速度，赛斯把直觉放在理智前面。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0347", "zh": "现在。你们只看见自己愿意看见的，而把暗示当作你们所见之物的结果或起因，那是愚蠢。在课堂上担心暗示会招致某个特定结果，也是愚蠢……因为正是暗示造成了你们所看见的一切。你们通过暗示与预期来形成你们的物质实相。你们在潜意识与意识的层面上，经验你们预期要经验的东西。因此，正如鲁柏极小心地不让暗示掺夹其中，他也让你们变得过分谨慎了；正因这个缘故，课堂上你们错失了许多机会……这些就是我今晚早些时候谈过的那些赌注。你们本有能力看见比你们实际所见的更多的东西，而你们是有这个能力的。你享受自己的被动状态（对[CW]说），到了欢喜交付、全然放手的地步；而其实，你们看，被动之中有一个点，在那里你是被动而警觉的。你却越过了那个点，于是失去了你本可以看见的东西。就像我们这位在场的朋友越过了那个点（指[TM]），看着那些肖像，然后有意识地……因为你并没有先做出原初的直觉判断……而是有意识地按国籍、年龄，以及你想到的种种条件，去端详那些肖像。", "en": "Now, you see what you are willing to see, and it is stupidity to consider suggestion as the result or the cause of what you see. It is stupidity in class to worry that suggestion would cause a given result... for suggestion causes whatever you see. You form your physical reality through suggestion and expectation. You experience what you expect to experience at a subconscious and a conscious level. And therefore as Ruburt is very careful that suggestion is not involved, so he has also had you be overly cautious, and there have been many opportunities in class that you have missed for this reason... and these are the bets that I have spoken about earlier this evening. You have the ability to see more than you saw, and you have the ability. You enjoyed your passivity (to CW) to the point of a joyous giving-up; and instead, you see, there is a point within passivity where you are passively alert. And you went beyond the point and lost what you might have seen. As our friend here went beyond the point (referring to TM), looked at the portraits and consciously... for you did not make an original intuitive judgment... but consciously looked at those portraits in terms of nationality, age, and all the requirements that you thought of.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第493节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "493", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0209", "zh": "你不会满意这名男性的，而且你在直觉上明了这一点。想要得到他的这份痴迷程度正好与你内心明白自己不想要他的了悟成正比，但是在寻觅他的过程中只有兴奋。你一定要停止寻觅，而对自己。", "en": "You would not be happy with the male, and you intuitively realize this. The obsession to have him grows precisely in proportion to your inner realization that you do not want him, but only the excitement involved in searching for him. You must end the search and face the self.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第329节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "329", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0617", "zh": "这并不是说，所有这种儿童都该被在家照顾，或，如果双亲受环境所迫，而将他们的子女放在一个机构里，就该觉得内疚。不过，在每个个别的案例里，父母的直觉常会指向最合适的方向。如果他们了解到，在这种情况背后的确有个理由，那么，单单是那个了悟，就能减轻父母的负担，而帮助他们决定在自己特定的例子里所要采取的路线。", "en": "This is not to say that all such children should be cared for at home, or that parents should feel guilty if they are forced through circumstances to place their offspring in an institution. The intuition of the parents, however, will often direct the most proper course in each individual case. If it is understood that there is indeed a reason behind such circumstances, then that realization alone can help ease the parents’ burden, and help them decide which course to take in their own particular case.", "source": "健康之道 · 第12节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "12", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0538", "zh": "在某些时代，尤其是当近代医药科学诞生的时候，对接种的信念——如果不是被老百姓相信，那么就是被医生们所相信——的确拥有新的暗示及希望的伟大力量，但我恐怕科学的医学其成绩曾经引起与它曾治愈的同样多的新病。当它救了命的时候，它能够这样做是因为医生本身直觉的治愈性了解，或因为病人是如此的被他所做的伟大努力所深深打动，因而，也间接的信服了他自己的价值。", "en": "At certain times, and most particularly at the birth of medical science in modern times, the belief in inoculation, if not by the populace then by the doctors, did possess the great strength of new suggestion and hope — but I am afraid that scientific medicine has caused as many new diseases as it has cured. When it saves lives, it does so because of the intuitive healing understanding of the physician, or because the patient is so impressed by the great efforts taken in his behalf, and therefore is convinced secondhandedly of his own worth.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第814节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "814", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0574", "zh": "那些“属性”就是想象、创造、心灵感应、千里眼和做梦的能力，以及逻辑与推理的机能。你知道你做梦，你知道你思考，那些是直接的经验。（停顿。）任何时候你用仪器探索进实相的本质时，不论那仪器多么精密，你都是在看一种二手的证据。举例来说，做梦的主观证据，比一个关于扩张中的宇宙、黑洞、甚至原子及分子本身的证据，要远较“令人信服”且不可推翻。虽然在许多方面，仪器的确可以是非常有利的，但它们给你的却仍只是二手而非一手的探查工具——而它们远比思想、感受与直觉的主观属性，更扭曲了实相的本质。", "en": "Those “properties” are the faculties of the imagination, creativity, telepathy, clairvoyance, and dreaming, as well as the functions of logic and reason. You know that you dream. You know that you think. Those are direct experiences. (Pause.) Anytime you use instruments to probe into the nature of reality, you are looking at a kind of secondary evidence, no matter how excellent the instruments may be. The subjective evidence of dreaming, for example, is far more “convincing” and irrefutable than is the evidence for an expanding universe, black holes, or even atoms and molecules themselves. Although instruments can indeed be most advantageous in many ways, they still present you with secondary rather than primary tools of investigation—and they distort the nature of reality far more than the subjective attributes of thoughts, feelings, and intuitions do.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第909节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "909", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0598", "zh": "也可以说，人处理思考在自然上的影响。他增益了其余的自然。（停顿。）因此他增加了不同类的精神组织，那是自然本身所要求、预期和欲愿的。动物并不读或写书，但它们的确经由它们经验的范畴，并经由直觉的知晓去直接「阅读」自然。人类的推理心给自然增加了一层大气（停顿。），比如说，那就与围绕着地球的辐射带一样的真实。", "en": "He deals with the effect of thinking upon nature, so to speak. He adds to the rest of nature. (Pause.) He therefore adds a different kind of mental organization — an organization, then, that nature itself requires, anticipates, and desires. Animals do not read or write books, but they do “read” nature directly through the context of their own experience, and through intuitive knowing. Man’s reasoning mind adds an atmosphere to nature (pause), that is as real, say, as the Van Allen Belts (or radiation fields) that surround the earth.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第8节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "8", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0545", "zh": "到某个程度，你的直觉引介你一件事实，即你在宇宙里有你自己的位置，而那宇宙本身是对你有好感的。那些直觉说出在那个宇宙的组织里，你独特而重要的角色。那些直觉知道宇宙偏向你这方。然而，你的推理力却只能处理你肉体感知的结果——至少以你们社会所容许它的训练而言。事实上，你不让你的推理力获得重要资料的结果，因为你曾教它不信任心灵的能力。孩子们的童话故事则仍携带着一些那种古老的知识。", "en": "To some extent or another, your intuitions acquaint you with the fact that you have your own place in the universe, and that the universe itself is well-disposed toward you. The intuitions speak of your unique and vital part in the fabric of that universe. The intuitions know that the universe bends in your direction. Your reasoning can deal only with results of your physical perception, however — at least with the training your societies have allowed it. You have in fact denied your reasoning the results of important data, for you have taught it to distrust the psychic faculties. Children’s fairy tales still carry some of that ancient knowledge.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第825节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "825", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "直觉是身体里的事，不只是念头", "note": "直觉只是心里想一想，这个说法赛斯不接受。第198节他说得很硬：直觉本身看来像是精神性的，其实也是行动，就其本身而论会造成肉体结构在化学与电磁层面的改变；这类直觉在人格处于梦境或出离状态时出现得特别多。第269节讲投射时一样：智力发挥了一定作用，但直觉的性质最重要，而投射发生时肉体会发生化学变化，还有电磁变化，随投射所采用的形式而定。《个人实相的本质》第675节给了一个双向的图：鲁柏的心智比脑对其他实相有更多觉察，而他意识地相信自己与自己感知的更大实相，脑因此向心智的活动尽量开放，于是某种直觉的、心灵的经验能被肉体感觉到——这份知识是通过身体感受的改变被诠释的，因而拿到一份重要的身体合法性；同一节他说广阔心智的经验会化解其他层面上知性与直觉之间任何似乎存在的冲突，身体组织借由感官资料新的混合去诠释那个统一，于是实质上这份资料就变得合理了。症状那一侧他记的是同一套账：改善随着人格直觉地学习而来，与时间基本上没关系——一种直觉的了悟可能突然出现，同时一批批症状也一样快速地消失，因为自发的那自己被允许更多自由，那正是直觉理解的根源（第321节）；当直觉被允许自由，它们会在睡觉时于治疗上帮助人格、使它焕然一新，用在令人兴奋的创造上的能量越多，能用在治疗上的就越多，症状被断了能量就活不成（第324节）；自我与直觉的自己之间的斗争确实跟着而来，但能量用对了，这些要素就会平衡（第324节）。《健康之道》第11节他说那些感受鼓励意识的表达，把本来可能被埋在紧张与恐惧之下的直觉性信息放出来，这种了悟有它自己生物上的效应，刺激身体所有的疗愈属性。《灵魂永生》第574节留了一项可练的能力：经过练习，你能变得直觉地觉察自己的内在肉体环境，就像觉察外在物质环境一样——你能感知你的肠子或你的手此刻的实相。《心灵的本质》第798节他管那叫身体拥有的一种无言的知识，它带来你的身体动作、造成身体反应那种壮观的精确，因此非常实际；怀着爱心去探索那些实相，会带你与你存在的内在次元直接接触，并提供最重要的直觉了解。《早期课》第8册第337节：人的创造力大部分透过双手直接展现，因此手常被用在治疗上，而手所包含的意义，内我可以直觉地感受到。第32节则给了一个身体层面的提醒：你有很强的直觉、而且速度快，但可以学习让身体放松一点。至于它为什么比逻辑快，《个人与群体事件的本质》第803节说：身体内在环境与天气模式之间有无数关系，那种古老的与暴风雨认同的感觉完全有效，在这个意义上感觉的真实性比逻辑的真实性高超得多——逻辑处理外在状况、处理因果关系，直觉处理最亲密那一类的切身经验，处理用你们的话说移动得远比光速还快的主观运动，也处理你们因果层面因为太慢而感知不到的同时性事件；内在环境的活动对你们太快，理性跟不上，但直觉能给你关于这种行为的线索。", "src": "《早期课》第1册第32节；第2册第269节；第4册第198节；第7册第321、324节；第8册第337节；《灵魂永生》第574节；《个人实相的本质》第675节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第803节；《心灵的本质》第798节；《健康之道》第11节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 32 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 269 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 198 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 321 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 324 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 337 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 574 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 675 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 803 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 798 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 11 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "直觉会改动身体", "note": "化学与电磁层面——赛斯把直觉算成一种行动。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0150", "zh": "在这样的情况下，这些觉知可能会以灵感或直觉的思想出现，而找到通往自我的方法。人格在梦境或出离的状况下，显然会出现许多这类的直觉。虽然直觉本身看起来像是精神性的，其实也是行动，而且就其本身而论，也会造成肉体结构化学及电磁层面的改变。", "en": "In such circumstances these perceptions may find their way to the ego, appearing as inspirations or intuitive thought. It is obvious that many such intuitions appear when the personality is in a dreaming state or in states of dissociation. The intuitions themselves, while seemingly mental, are action, and as such they produce changes in the physical organism, both chemical and electromagnetic.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第198节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "198", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0181", "zh": "总而言之，智力发挥了一定作用，但直觉性质是最重要的。当投射发生时，肉体会发生化学变化。还有电磁变化。这些变化是根据投射时采用的形式而定。", "en": "All in all the intellect plays some part, but the intuitional qualities are the most important. There are chemical changes that occur with the physical body when projections occur. There are also electromagnetic variations. These vary according to the form in which the projection occurs.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第269节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "269", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0457", "zh": "鲁柏的心智比他的脑对其他实相有更多的觉察，但他有意识地相信“他自己与他感知的更大实相”。脑也拥有这个信念，因此，它把自己向着心智活动尽量开放。因为它这样做，所以到了某个程度，某种直觉的心灵及“广阔的知性”经验能被肉体感觉到。这个知识是通过身体感受的改变而被诠释的，因而给了这个知识重要的身体合法性。在这种情形里，高度的精神与心灵活动反映在身体的经验里，提供了有益的统一。", "en": "Now: Ruburt’s mind is far more aware of other realities than his brain is, but he consciously believes in the greater reality of himself and his perceptions. The brain also possesses this belief, and so it opens itself as much as possible to the mind’s activities. Because it does, certain intuitive psychic and “intellectually spacious” experiences can be physically felt to some extent. The knowledge is interpreted through alterations in body sensation, which give it an important corporeal validity. In such cases high mental and psychic activity is reflected in the body’s experience, providing a beneficial unity.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第675节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "675", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0459", "zh": "用到广阔心智的经验，可以化解其他层面发生在知性与直觉之间任何似乎存在的冲突。不论到什么可能的程度时，这个身体的组织通过感官资料新的混合来诠释那个统一，因此实质地，这个资料就很合理了。", "en": "(Long pause at 11:05, eyes closed.) Experience with the spacious mind dissolves any seeming conflicts that occur between the intellect and the intuitions at other levels. To whatever extent possible, the physical organism interprets that unity through a new mixture of sense data, so that materially the information makes sense.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第675节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "675", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "症状与治疗这一侧", "note": "直觉给了，症状退；能量被堵，症状活。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0201", "zh": "过敏正在消失。随着人格凭着直觉学习，而有了改善，你知道，与时间基本上没有任何关系。一种直觉的理解可能会突然出现，同时一批批症状也一样快速地消失。自发的自己现在被允许更多的自由，这是直觉理解的根源。", "en": "The sensitivities are vanishing. Improvements come as the personality learns intuitively, you see, having nothing to do with time in a basic manner. An intuitive grasp may come suddenly with an equally fast disappearance of blocks of symptoms. The spontaneous self is being allowed more freedom now, this is the source of the intuitional understanding.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第321节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "321", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0206", "zh": "能够用来吸收一些白天被误导的能量那种刺激不再可得。自己露出了它的真实面目。当直觉被允许自由，你看，它们就会在睡觉时在治疗上帮助人格，使它焕然一新。鲁柏使用越多能量在令人兴奋的创造上，你知道，能够用在治疗目的上的能量就会越多。不给症状能量，它们就无法存活。", "en": "The stimuli that can be used to absorb some of the misdirected energy in the day is no longer available. The self shows its true face. When the intuitions are allowed freedom you see they therapeutically aid the personality in sleep and refresh it. The more energy that is used on Ruburts part in exciting creative ways, the more is available, you see, for therapeutic purposes. The symptoms are denied energy and cannot survive.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第324节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "324", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0208", "zh": "我告诉过你，自我与直觉的自己之间的斗争这里随之而来，但是正确使用能量，这些要素就会平衡。", "en": "The struggle between the ego and intuitional self follows here as I have told you, but with the correct use of energy these elements are balanced.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第324节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "324", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0616", "zh": "那些感受的确鼓励意识的表达，并释放否则可能会埋在紧张和恐惧下的直觉性信息。这种了悟有它们自己生物上的效应，刺激身体所有的疗愈属性——也轻易地将心智推向“更高的”组织，在其中理解到，生命所有仿佛的不足都得到了弥补。", "en": "Those feelings do indeed encourage expression of consciousness, and release intuitive information that may otherwise be buried beneath tensions and fears. Such realizations have their own biological effects, stimulating all of the healing properties of the body — and also easily propelling the mind toward “higher” organizations, in which all of life’s seeming inadequacies are understood to be redeemed.", "source": "健康之道 · 第11节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "11", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0032", "zh": "这应该是有益的。同时，你开始通过瑜伽练习培养的缓慢的呼吸习惯也将是有益的。戒掉抽烟习惯在这方面对你也有帮助。你有很强的直觉，而且速度快，但你可以学习让身体放松一点。目前的人格直接源自于早期的环境，而这个个性又逐渐养成一种恐惧。鲁柏担心的是，如果他不尽快行动，就象征而言，他将会被逮住而变成跛脚，就象他现在的母亲一样。", "en": "This should be of benefit. Also the slow breathing habits you began to acquire with your yoga exercises will be beneficial. Giving up the smoking habit will also help you in this respect. You are strongly intuitive and very quick, but you can learn to have a more relaxed body. A fear has been developed by the present personality resulting directly from early circumstances. Ruburt is afraid that if he does not operate quickly he will be symbolically caught and crippled as is the case with his present mother.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第32节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "32", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "身体本来就有的那种知", "note": "比光速还快的那一层，身体一直在处理。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0535", "zh": "在身体的内在环境与天气模式之间，存在着无以数计的关系。古老的与暴风雨认同的感觉是十分合理的，而那样说的话，感觉的“真实性”是比逻辑的真实性要高超多了。当一个人自觉是暴风雨的一部分时，那些感觉说的是一件真真实实的事。逻辑是处理外在的状况，处理因果关系，而直觉是处理最亲密的切身经验，处理以你们的话来说移动得远比光速还快的主观运动与活动，以及处理你们的因果层面因为太慢而感知不到的同时性事件。（注二。）", "en": "There are innumerable relationships that exist between the interior environment of the body and the weather patterns. The ancient feelings of identification with storms are quite valid, and in that respect the “realism” of feelings is far superior to the realism of logic. When a person feels a part of a storm, those feelings speak a literal truth. Logic deals with exterior conditions, with cause-and-effect relationships. Intuitions deal with immediate experience of the most intimate nature, with subjective motions and activities that in your terms move far quicker than the speed of light, and with simultaneous events that your cause-and-effect level is far too slow to perceive.2", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第803节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "803", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0536", "zh": "就那方面而言，内在环境的活动对你们来说是太快了，你们在理性上无法跟得上它，然而你们的直觉可以给你们有关这种行为的线索。一个国家应对它自己的旱灾，地震，水灾，暴风雨负责——也为它自己的收获及丰饶的各色产品以及它的工业与文化上的成就负责，而所有这些都是彼此相关的。", "en": "In that regard also, the activities of the inner environment are too fast for you to follow intellectually. Your intuitions, however, can give you clues to such behavior. A country is responsible for its own droughts, earthquakes, floods, hurricanes — and for its own harvests and rich display of products, its industry and cultural achievements, and each of these elements is related to each other one.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第803节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "803", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0404", "zh": "你可以感知你的肠子或你的手存在的此刻的实相；经过练习，你也能体验在你肉体内同时存在的当下片刻的内在宁静与骚动。这使你生出无量的赞赏与惊欢，并且与组成你身体的活的肉体物质有一种统一和谐的感觉。经过练习你能变得直觉性地觉察你的内在肉体环境，就与觉察外在物质环境一样。", "en": "You can perceive the moment’s reality as it exists for your intestine, or your hand; and experience, with practice, the present inner peace and commotion that exist simultaneously within your physical body. This brings a great appreciation and wonder, a sense of unity with the living corporeal material of which you are physically composed. With practice you can become as intuitively aware of your internal physical environment, as [of] your external physical environment.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第574节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "574", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0531", "zh": "这是一种身体拥有的无言的知识，带来你身体的动作，并造成了身体反应的壮观的精确性。那么，它是非常实际的。以你们的话来说，形成世界的同样力量，现在形成你们的主观实相，且是自然宇宙的一个源头。怀着爱心探索那些实相，将带你进入与你的存在之内在次元的直接接触，并提供最重要的直觉了解。", "en": "This is the kind of wordless knowledge the body possesses, that brings forth your physical motion and results in the spectacular preciseness of bodily response. It is, then, highly practical. In your terms, the same force that formed the world forms your subjective reality now, and is a source of the natural universe. Exploring those realities lovingly will bring you into direct contact with inner dimensions of your being, providing intuitive understandings that are of greatest import.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第798节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "798", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0217", "zh": "人类的创造力大部分都是透过双手直接展现，因此就经常用在治疗上。双手所包含的意义，内我可以直觉感受到。", "en": "Much of man's creativity is expressed directly through his hands, and for this reason they are often used in healing experiences. They have a significance intuitively felt by the inner self.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第342节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "342", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "创作、发明与那些「意外」", "note": "赛斯把灵感拆成可观察的过程。科学那边：最伟大的科学发现永远是意外，它们来自直觉性的创造——突然之间，一种先前无法预知的新的重要意义被看到了；而你们接受所有适合自己理论的资料，忽略相反的线索（《未知的实相》卷一第694节）。他举爱因斯坦：那人能相当自然地与宇宙种种机能认同，能倾听物质的内在声音，被直觉性与情感性地引导到他的发现上——他背靠着时间，而感觉到它让步且动摇了（第701节）。同一节他说你们这最近的冒险里正在发现外在的操纵不够，光是科技不是那个答案，而他补一句：有爱心的科技并没有错。数学那一头他也碰过：那些概念模式是以直觉的数学语言给出的，根本不在一个精确而狭窄的范围里，却回答了比所提问题更深的问题（《早期课》第9册第462节）。工业与科技的整体来源他归给梦：你们所有制造出来的东西也源自梦的领域，人天生就有那些尚待发展的能力，有关它们的暗示永远在梦境、艺术、宗教甚至科学里出现，在政治与商业里则作为大半未显现的直觉背景而被忽略（《梦、进化与价值完成》第890节）；从印刷术到爱迪生的发明都是梦中灵感的直接显现（第890节）；第934节他说得更狠——外面那个科技世界曾经就是梦的世界，让工业世界成为可能的发现与发明一直潜伏在人的心智里，代表可能性的一份内在闪亮风景，人透过梦的利用把它带入实现。创作这边他给的是可操作的说法：在看似没有方向、非常抽象的散乱与能量背后其实有方向存在，无法从理智上觉知，却可以从直觉上感受到，而这正是你自己的艺术与所有创意背后的那股力量（《早期课》第8册第418节）；如果你直觉地意识到那种奇迹般的工整，允许自己被那个特定的片刻点包围，画作就会围绕你成形，方式有点像透过鲁柏的声音形成我（第401节）；对艺术家或诗人来说找到这个自己的中心要容易些，直觉的象征较易辨认——你可以抓住一幅画原来的灵感顺着它向外而行，也可以看自己的成品顺着它向内回到它的源头（第9册第451节）。他反复强调顺序不能倒：谈梦的书应该完成，是因为直觉的自己已被释放到足以使这件事成为并且提供了方法；怨气与书本身没有连结，反而阻碍了书的发展（第7册第324节）。有些人的节奏本来就是阵发式的：奥蒂斯这个人格靠一阵一阵的大突进发展，直觉汹涌而来，他必须学会处置它们，有时候压得他不堪重负（第9册第504节）。他也算过大账：那种经验在最强时能把直觉知识从私人的领域推出来，改变文明，而那份难以置信的能量永远在最初的经验里，所有其他的发展都由它而来（《灵魂永生》第596节）；他甚至还说过一切创造与意识都诞生于游戏的特性而非工作的特性，诞生于加快了的直觉性自发性（第518节）。第350节他给两人一颗定心丸：仍然在为你们效劳的那种很强烈的东西，是创造力的直觉本性，它总会在某个方式上让事实恢复清楚的全貌。最后他把这套分工算到自己出的书上：《早期课》之外的那些书里，一些强调创意、直觉与想象力的运用，却相对没有清楚的推理、逻辑或对传统的尊重，作者因此一直处在一种创造性的张力里；而他说他们这一套书要做的是把知性与直觉的力量合在一起，用这个办法把新概念放进现存的世界（《神奇之道》第12节）。", "src": "《未知的实相》卷一第694、701节；《早期课》第7册第324节；第8册第418、401、350节；第9册第462、451、504节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第890、934节；《灵魂永生》第596、518节；《神奇之道》第12节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 694 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 701 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 324 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 418 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 401 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 350 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 462 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 451 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 504 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 890 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 934 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 596 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 518 节"}, {"n": 14, "id": null, "label": "第 12 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "科学那边", "note": "他发现被称为「意外」，其实是直觉先看见了新的意义。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0470", "zh": "最伟大的科学发现永远是“意外”，它们是来自直觉性的创造，是当突然之间“先前”无法预知的一种新的重要意义被看到了。你们接受所有适合你们理论的资料，而忽略了相反的线索，然而，在这所有之下，你们是“创造重要意义”的生物，是“模式形成者”，沉浸在时间里，却基本上与时间分开，因而，新的洞见进入你的觉察里而真的改变了在任何既定时候，任何既定实相的特质。", "en": "The greatest scientific discoveries are always “accidents.” They come from intuitional creativity, when suddenly a new kind of significance is seen that was not “earlier” predictable. You accept all data that fit your theories, and ignore clues to the contrary. Yet underneath it all you are significance-making creatures, pattern-formers, immersed in time but basically apart from it, and so new insights come into your awareness and literally change the quality of any given reality at any given time.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第694节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "694", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0471", "zh": "爱因斯坦那个人虽然与你们自己的文明相连，但在这一点上却最接近上段所言的，因为他能相当自然的与宇宙的种种“机能”认同，能倾听物质的内在声音，而被直觉性与情感性地引导到他的发现上。他背靠着时间，而感觉到它让步且动摇了。", "en": "While connected with your own civilization, the man Einstein1 came closest perhaps in this regard, for he was able to quite naturally identify himself with various “functions” of the universe. He was able to listen to the inner voice of matter. He was intuitively and emotionally led to his discoveries. He leaned against time, and felt it give and wobble.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第701节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "701", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0472", "zh": "现在：即使以你们的历史及顺序性时间的说法，作为一个族类，你们已尝试过与物质世界打交道的种种方法。在这个最近的冒险里，你们正在发现外在的操纵是不够的，而光是科技并不是“那答案”。请了解我的意思：一个有爱心的科技并没有错。", "en": "Now: Even in your terms of history and serial time, as a race you have tried various methods of dealing with the physical world.6 In this latest venture you are discovering that exterior manipulation is not enough, that technology alone is not “the answer.” Please understand me: There is nothing wrong with a loving technology. If Einstein had been a better mathematician,7 he would not have made the breakthroughs that he did. He would have been too cowed. Yet even then his mathematics did hold him back, and put a kink in his intuitions. Often you take it for granted that intuitive knowledge is not practical, will not work, or will not give you diagrams. Those same diagrams of which science is so proud, however, can also be barriers, giving you a dead instead of a living knowledge. Therefore, they can be quite impractical.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第701节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "701", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0323", "zh": "那些数学资料我也已经作了某种程度的说明。这比较困难，因为鲁柏欠缺数学词汇，而且那些概念模式是以直觉的数学语言给出的——根本不在一个精确而狭窄的范围里，并且回答了比所提问题更深的问题。不过我相信，那些特定问题的答案就内在于所给出的资料里，一经参照便会显明。", "en": "The mathematical data I have also somewhat explained. This is more difficult because of Ruburt’s lack of mathematical vocabulary, and the fact that conceptual patterns were given in intuitive mathematical language—not in a precise narrow range at all, and answering deeper questions than those asked. Nevertheless the answers to the particular questions are inherent within the material given, I believe, and become obvious by reference.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第462节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "462", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0568", "zh": "梦对农业的发展负责，对工业、对国家的兴亡、对那曾为罗马的“光荣”以及罗马的毁灭也一样。（停顿。）你们目前科技的进步，可几乎直溯到印刷术的发明，到爱迪生的发明，那是梦中灵感的直接显现。但如果我现在告诉你们是真的，那么很显然，当我说你们的物质世界是源自梦世界，我必然是指与通常对梦实相的定义非常不同的东西。再次的，我可以选择另一个用语，但我想强调每个人与那另一个实相的密切联系，那实相的确发生在你们所认作的梦境里（全都很热切的）。", "en": "They were responsible for the birth of agriculture, as well as industry, the rise and fall of nations, the “glory” that was Rome, and Rome’s destruction. (Pause.) Your present technological advances can almost be dated from the [invention of] the printing press, to Edison’s inventions, which were flashes of intuition, dream-inspired. But if what I am telling you is true, then it is obvious that when I say that your physical world originated in the world of dreams, I must mean something far different from the usual definition of dream reality. Again, I could choose another term, but I want to emphasize each person’s intimate contact with that other reality that does occur in what you think of as the state of dreaming (all very intently).", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第890节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "890", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0586", "zh": "那么，在梦境之中，家庭、社区与国家的需要及愿望是广为人知的。梦境是世界知识的一个丰富来源，因而也为其科技的自然发展负责。这是极为重要的一点，因为“在外面的科技世界”曾一度是梦的世界。那使得工业世界变得可能的发现及发明，一直潜伏在人类心智里，代表了可能性的一个内在的闪亮风景，而人透过梦的利用将之带入实现——那曾一度为潜在的，对物质之直觉的及有意识的操纵。", "en": "In the dreaming state, then, the needs and desires of families, communities and countries are well known. The dream state serves as a rich source for the world’s knowledge, and is also therefore responsible for the outgrowth of its technology. This is a highly important point, for “the technological world out there” was at one time the world of dreams. The discoveries and inventions that made the industrial world possible were always latent in man’s mind, and represented an inner glittering landscape of probability that he brought into actualization through the use of dreams—the intuitive and the conscious manipulation of material that was at one time latent.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第934节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "934", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0567", "zh": "你们所有的制成品也是源自梦的领域，显然它们最先是被抽象的构思，而以相同的方式，人造出他最先的工具。人天生具有（停顿良久）所有那些能力——给予他特征的能力——以及那些以你们的说法尚待发展的能力。并非他到现在还没用它们，而是在你们所认为的文明之连续性主线上，他还没关注于它们。有关那些能力的暗示，永远在梦境，在艺术、宗教、甚至科学里出现。它们出现在政治与商业里，却是作为大半未显现的直觉背景，而大半被忽略。我们在此书稍后会回到这上面去。", "en": "All of your manufactured objects also originated in the realm of dreams, first obviously being conceived of mentally, and in the same way man produced his first tools. He was born with (long pause) all of those abilities—abilities by which he is now characterized—and with other abilities that in your terms still wait for development. Not that he has not used them so far, but that he has not focused upon them in what you consider the main lines of civilized continuity. Hints of those abilities are always present in the dream state, and in the arts, in the religions, and even in the sciences. They appear in politics and business, but as the largely unmanifest intuitive background, which is largely ignored. We will return to these later in the book.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第890节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "890", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "艺术与写作这边", "note": "灵感可以顺着走：从原初的那一下向外，或从成品向内回到源头。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0267", "zh": "这个练习对于克服这个问题会很管用，因为你够坚强，也需要内在的自由。在这种看似没有方向、非常抽象的散乱和能量背后，其实有它的方向存在，虽然无法从理智上觉知到，但可以从直觉上感受到。这就是你自己的艺术和所有创意背后的那股力量。（停顿） 它甚至可以用来作为创造的架构，因为你可以从这些原始资料中，按照自己的目的来创造和引导能量。你可以接收这种喧扰并加以利用，但如果你把自己设定成跟它对对抗的立场，那就没辙了，如此一来，你就会受到威胁。", "en": "The exercise will do much to override this, for you are strong enough and you need inner freedom. There is behind such seemingly undirected, abstract tumult and energy, direction that cannot be intellectually perceived, but can be intuitively sensed. And this is the force that is behind your own art and all creativity. (Pause.) It can even serve as a framework for creativity, for from these raw materials you can forge and direct energy for your own purposes. You can take that tumult and use it, but not if you set yourself up against it. Then, it is threatening to you.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第418节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "418", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0252", "zh": "无论何时，形式都是由能量的特定条件所引发。如果你直觉地意识到那种奇迹般的工整，如果你允许自己受到那个特定片刻点的包围，那么就会透过你形成一幅画作，其方式就有点类似透过鲁柏的声音形成我一样。不过，你的画作当然更加显眼。", "en": "The form is caused by a characteristic condition of the energy at any given time. If you are intuitively aware of that miraculous neatness, if you allow yourself to be enveloped within that particular moment point, then the painting will form itself about you in somewhat the same manner that I am formed about Ruburt's voice. But your painting of course will be more visible.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第401节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "401", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0294", "zh": "对艺术家或诗人来说，找到这个自己的中心要容易些。直觉的象征较易辨认。你可以抓住一幅画原来的灵感，顺着它向外而行；也可以看你自己的成品，顺着它向内回到它的源头。你跟上我了吗？", "en": "It is somewhat easier for the artist or poet to find this center of the self. The intuitive symbols can be better recognized. Now you can grab a hold of the original inspiration for a painting, and ride it outward, or you can look at your own completed painting and ride it inward to its source. Do you follow me?", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第451节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "451", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0368", "zh": "我们开始学到“游戏”的创造性喜悦。例如，我相信所有的创造与意识是诞生于游戏的特性而非工作的特性，诞生于加快了的直觉性的自发性中，在我自己所有的存在中，以及我所知的别人的经验中这都是不变的常态。", "en": "We are beginning to learn the creative joy of play. I believe, for example, that all creativity and consciousness is born in the quality of play, as opposed to work, in the quickened intuitional spontaneity that I see as a constant through all my own existences, and in the experience of those I know.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第518节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "518", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0416", "zh": "这种经验在它们最强的时候，能从私人的领域把直觉知识推出来以改变文明。那不可置信的能量永远是在最初的经验里，在它内含有浓缩的能量，所有其他的发展都由之而来。", "en": "At their strongest, such experiences can propel intuitive knowledge from the private domain to change civilization. The incredible charge is always in the initial experience. Contained within it is the condensed energy from which all other developments come.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第596节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "596", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0357", "zh": "奥蒂斯的人格，其本性就是靠一阵一阵的大突进来发展的：直觉汹涌而来，而他必须学会处置它们。有时候那些直觉压得他不堪重负。从一世蹦进另一世、连性别也换掉——这正合他的做派。", "en": "Otis’s personality attains developments by its nature in great spurts and starts; intuitions; and then he must learn to handle them. At times they overburden him. It was like him to leap from one life into another, with a change of sex.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第504节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "504", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0204", "zh": "直觉的自己现在已被释放到足以使这件事成为可能，而且提供了方法，你看。谈梦的书应该要完成了。怨气与书本身没有连结，而且事实上阻碍了书的发展。", "en": "The intuitive self' is now freed enough to make this possible, and provide the way, you see. The dream book should be finished. The resentment was not connected with the book per se, and in fact hampered the book's development.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第324节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "324", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0220", "zh": "鲁柏应该可以继续工作，尽管身体上相当无能为力。但是，这些状况本来不太可能出现。你们两个都有某种很强烈的特质，这个特质仍然非常明显，能为你们效劳且提供协助，那就是创造力的直觉本性，应该会以某种方式，让事实恢复清楚的全貌。", "en": "Ruburt would have continued to work, though physically quite incapacitated. These conditions however would not likely have resulted. You both had something very strong working for you, still strong enough to help, and that was the creative intuitive nature, which would have in one way or another made the facts plain.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第350节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "350", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "这套资料自己的写法", "note": "赛斯把知性与直觉的并用，当成他出书的方法本身。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0602", "zh": "在另一方面，许多Parker书则强调创意、直觉、想象力的利用，但却相对地没有任何清楚的推理、逻辑，或根本没有对传统的尊重。在这里，我予以简化了，以表明我的意思。那么，在某个程度来看，Prentice就是总是处于一种创造性的张力，因为看似相反的、看似矛盾的成分，都透过这些部门来表达。", "en": "Many of the Parker books on the other hand emphasize creativity, the intuitions, the use of the imagination, but are relatively innocent of any clear reasoning, logic, or any feeling for tradition at all. I am simplifying here to some extent to make my point. Prentice is always, then, to some extent in a state of creative tension, as the seemingly opposed, seemingly contradictory elements are each expressed through these two divisions.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第12节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "12", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0604", "zh": "我们的书，借由将知性和直觉的力量合在一起，试图将新概念嵌入现存的世界里——换言之，借由将Prentice的两个极端带到一起。", "en": "Our books are attempting to insert new ideas into the world as it now is, by combining the powers of the intellect and the powers of the intuitions — in other words, by closing the two ends of Prentice’s extremes.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第12节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "12", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B10", "title": "人人都有的那一层，包括孩子与老人", "note": "赛斯一再讲直觉不是少数人的装置，而是意识本来的工作方式，只是多数人不给它意识的身份。每个人都知道自己的经验有其重要性，都有一个把自己联系着更大创造模式的隐秘目的，而许多人因为那内在目标没被有意识地知道而充满困扰（《心灵的本质》第752节）。几乎每个人都有过意识上的古怪经验，并直觉地知道自己更大的经验不限于物质实相的范围（《灵魂永生》第570节）；每个人直觉上都知道自己参与了梦行动那个领域（《早期课》第4册第149节）；许多人直觉地了解自己是成群而非单一的，那份了解通常被放进转世的说法里（《未知的实相》卷二第721节），而自性若至少没有直觉地了解这份传承，它就比较贫乏（第731节）。他说那些被别人选出来的灵媒式人物，向外显示的正是所有人直觉地知晓的内在真理（《灵魂永生》第585节）；也给了普通人一条：诚实地为自己发声，你便也为他人发声，而他人直觉地知道这一点（《早期课》第9册第465节）。连梦那个被意识心认为愚蠢不理性的世界，也是内我精心建构的，那种精确只有透过直觉才能获得——而每一个个体都知道（第3册第92节）。这一层从出生前就在：孩子不是空空等着吸水的一块海绵，它已经吸满了知识；到某程度，子宫里的孩子已经直觉到母亲的信念与信息，因而被设定程序，以某种模式来行为或成长（《心灵的本质》第771节）。第824节他写得最动人：孩子带着出生时由架构二提供的原动力与支持能量，直觉地知道那些有利于他发展的愿望比无益的更容易发生；当他按那些内在冲动行动，他觉察到一种缓冲与支撑——孩子天生是诚实的，生病时他直觉地知道理由，而且十分明白是他自己带来了那个病。长大以后你与自己的天性认同，直觉地了解你的存在沉浸在成长的过程里、是它的一部分（第821节）。赛斯还用直觉替谁算聪明重新判分：有些人成熟、聪明地察觉自己与他人的感受，直觉地知道如何处理关系，甚至是很好的父母，可他们若不符合某些人造的理智标准，就可能被视为智障（《梦、进化与价值完成》第914节）。老人那一例更刺：他们想逃离安养院那些像壁橱一样的小房间时，常常比囚禁他们的亲人或社会更神智清楚，因为他们直觉地认出自由的需要，感得到那份被否定给他们与土地的神秘一体感（《个人实相的本质》第661节）。最后是他最常被误解的一段。他把理性属于男人、直觉属于女人这套分工当成一份需要撤销的账：你们想象男人是攻击性的、主动的、有头脑逻辑的、文明的建造者，于是把自我认同为男性，无意识就显得女性，女性特质被指派为消极、直觉、滋养，而你们还把直觉成分看得相当吓人，好像它们能以未知的方式爆炸、扰乱已知的模式（《心灵的本质》第765节）。他直接说：一个女人就和一个男人一样地具有理性，一个男人就和一个女人一样地具有直觉；你选择你的性别焦点是有理由的，那理由跟意识的弹性有关（《未知的实相》卷一第704节）。因为这套专门化，知性仿佛与直觉分开，敌对似乎出现在本来没有敌对的地方（第772节）；具直觉性或某种艺术天分的男人常因此自认为同性恋者，不管他是不是；而那些兴趣超出被当作女性范围的女人，她们表现直觉能力的尝试常常变成「不合理的」行为（第773节）。大艺术家不管那一套：任何时代、任何领域的伟大艺术家，直觉地感到一种超出特定性别的私人人性（第771节）。", "src": "《心灵的本质》第752、765、771、772、773节；《灵魂永生》第570、585节；《早期课》第3册第92节；第4册第149节；第9册第465节；《未知的实相》卷一第704节；卷二第721、731节；《个人与群体事件的本质》第821、824节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第914节；《个人实相的本质》第661节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 752 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 765 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 771 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 772 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 773 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 570 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 585 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 92 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 149 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 465 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 704 节"}, {"n": 12, "id": null, "label": "第 721 节"}, {"n": 13, "id": null, "label": "第 731 节"}, {"n": 14, "id": null, "label": "第 821 节"}, {"n": 15, "id": null, "label": "第 824 节"}, {"n": 16, "id": null, "label": "第 914 节"}, {"n": 17, "id": null, "label": "第 661 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "不用学也知道的东西", "note": "赛斯说的是一种人人都有、只是不被承认的知识。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0508", "zh": "每个人都直觉地知道自己的经验有其重要性，而且有某种意义，联系着个人与更大的创造模式。每个人偶尔都会感知一个私密的目的，但许多人却因为没能有意识地知道或清楚地觉察那内在的目标，而充满了困扰。", "en": "(9.35.) Each person knows intuitively that his or her own experiences somehow matter, and that there is a meaning, however obscured, that connects the individual with a greater creative pattern. Each person senses now and then a private purpose, and yet many are filled with frustration because that inner goal is not consciously known or clearly apprehended.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第752节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "752", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0398", "zh": "所有这些并不如它看起来那么玄秘。几乎每个人都有意识上的古怪经验，而直觉地知道他们更大的经验是不受限于物质实相的范围内的。大半的梦是像你从一个你大部分已遗忘了的旅程带回来的有生命的风景明信片。你的意识已经再次地定位于物质实相了，而那个梦是个把更深的经历转译为可认识的形式的企图。梦中形象也是极度“密码式”的，是潜藏在梦底下的事件的信号，这事件基本上是无法破解的。", "en": "(Pause at 9:23.) All of this is not as esoteric as it might seem. Almost every individual has had bizarre experiences with consciousness, and knows intuitively that their greater experience is not limited to physical reality. Most dreams are like animated postcards brought back from a journey that you have returned from and largely forgotten. Your consciousness is already oriented again to physical reality; the dream, an attempt to translate the deeper experience into recognizable forms. The images within the dream are also highly coded, and are signals for underlying events that are basically not decipherable.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第570节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "570", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0127", "zh": "对大多数人来说，这样的审查过程有其价值，因为可以防止人格被那些它没有能力处理的资料淹没。进一步的发展趋势就是，有能力留住其他场域获得的经验。无论如何，你们对于这个梦行动的领域，至少已有某种程度的认识，而每个人直觉上都知道自己参与其中。", "en": "For most people this censoring process is valuable, since it prevents the personality from being snowed under by data it is not equipped to handle. The ability to retain experience gained within other fields is the trend of further development. You are at least however to some extent familiar with this field of dream action, and every man intuitively knows his involvement here.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第149节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "149", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0410", "zh": "其实这些人被其他的人选了出来，以向外显示所有人直觉地知晓的内在真理。这儿有许多层次的重要性。在一方面来说，这种个人由他们同伴那儿收到他们的超自然能力与力量，容纳它并在物质世界展示它给所有的人看。他们扮演那受祝福的“内我”的角色。没有肉体的“外衣”，那“内我”实际上无法在物质实相里运作。不过，这能量是由“内我”而来的十分有效的投射。（停顿良久）", "en": "Now these people are chosen by others to manifest outwardly the interior truths that all intuitively know. There are many levels of significance here. On the one hand, such individuals receive their unearthly abilities and power from their fellows, contain it, exhibit it in the physical world for all to see. They play the part of the blessed inner self that actually cannot operate within physical reality uncloaked by flesh. This energy, however, is a quite valid projection from the interior self. (Long pause.)", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第585节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "585", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0486", "zh": "许多人直觉的了解“自己”是成群而非单一的。那个了解通常被放在转世的说法里，所以，“自己”被视为旅行过世纪，走过生死门而进入其它的时间与地方。", "en": "Many people realize intuitively that the self is multitudinous and not singular. The realization is usually put in reincarnational terms, so that the self is seen as traveling through the centuries, moving through doors of death and life into other times and places.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第721节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "721", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0488", "zh": "当自性没有直觉的了解这传承时，它是比较贫乏的。", "en": "Selfhood is poorer when it does not at least intuitively understand this heritage.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第731节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "731", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0328", "zh": "所以，就让先知是你们自己，却又让他同时代表所有其他人。诚实地为你们自己发声，你们便也为他人发声，而他人会直觉地知道这一点。", "en": "Let the prophet therefore be yourself, and yet let him also stand for every other man. In speaking honestly for yourself, you therefore speak also for others, and intuitively they know this.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第465节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "465", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "孩子、老人与艺术家", "note": "他把证据放在最不被当成「有知识」的那些人身上。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0542", "zh": "在孩子们熟悉传统的罪与罚概念之前，他们发现借希望带来好的事件要比带来不快乐的事更容易。孩子出生时就带来由“架构二”提供给他的原动力与支持能量，而他直觉的知道那些对他的发展有利的愿望比那些无益的较易“发生”。他天然的原动力自然引导他去发展他的身心，而当他按照那些内在冲动行动时，他觉察到一种保护效果与支持。孩子天生是诚实的，当他生了病时他直觉的知道其理由，而他十分明白是他自己带来了那个病。", "en": "Before children are acquainted with conventional ideas of guilt and punishment, they realize that it is easier to bring about good events, through wishing, than it is to bring about unhappy ones. The child carries with him [or her] the impetus and supporting energy provided him at birth from Framework 2, and he knows intuitively that desires conducive to his development “happen” easier than those that are not. His natural impulses naturally lead him toward the development of his body and mind, and he is aware of a cushioning effect and support as he acts in accordance with those inner impulses. The child is innately honest. When he gets sick he intuitively knows the reason why, and he knows quite well that he brought about the illness.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第824节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "824", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0512", "zh": "不过，孩子生下来并不是一块海绵，空白而准备好吸收知识。它已吸满了知识。可以说，有些将浮到表面，而被有意识的利用；有些则否。我在这儿说的是，到某程度，孩子在母胎中已经直觉到母亲的信念和信息，而到某程度上，它是「被设定程序」以某种模式来行为，或因而将以某种模式来成长。", "en": "The child is not born a sponge, however, empty but ready to soak up knowledge. It is already soaked in knowledge. Some will come to the surface, so to speak, and be used consciously. Some will not. I am saying here that to some extent the child in the womb is aware of the mother’s beliefs and information, and that to some extent (underlined) it is “programmed” to behave in a certain fashion, or to grow in a certain fashion as a result.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第771节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "771", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0539", "zh": "从一个婴儿长大到一个完全的成人，也许是你在此生所完成的最困难却又最容易的伟积。当你是个孩子的时候，你与你自己的天性认同，你直觉的了解到你的存在是沉浸在成长的过程里，并且是其一部分。", "en": "Now: Dictation: You are, of course, a part of nature, and a part of nature’s source. Growing from an infant to a full adult was probably one of the most difficult, and yet the most easy of feats that you will ever accomplish in a life. As a child you identified with your own nature. You intuitively realized that your being was immersed in and a part of the process of growth.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第821节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "821", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0579", "zh": "其他人也许是成熟的，聪明地察觉他们自己及其他人的感受，直觉的知道如何处理关系。作为成人，他们甚至是最好的父母——然而，如果他们不符合某些人造的理智标准，他们可能会被视为智障。他们实际上是与先前提及的人一样，只不过是在另一端的同等地位。", "en": "Other people may be sophisticated, brilliantly aware of their own feelings and those of other people, intuitively knowledgeable in the handling of relationships, even, as adults, exquisite parents—yet they may be labeled as retarded if they do not live up to certain artificial intellectual standards. They are actually in the same position at the other end as the people mentioned earlier.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第914节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "914", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0447", "zh": "然而，在你们的医院里，把病人从他们的自然环境里“提”了出来，而常常否定了他们动物性的安适，在医院里也很少涉及情感。（长久的停顿。）老年人在想逃离老人院像壁橱一样的小房间的努力中，常常以他们的方式显得比那些囚禁他们的亲人或社会更为神智清楚。 因为他们直觉地认出“自由的需要”，感觉到缺乏与土地的神秘的一体感，而这个感觉是他们被否定去拥有的。（见第十三章第六五〇节。）", "en": "In your hospitals however you take your patients out of their natural environment, and often deny them the comforts of creaturehood. There is little emotional involvement. (Long pause.) The senile, in their efforts to run away from their closeted rooms in sanitariums, often show far greater sanity in their way than the relative or society who imprisoned them. For they intuitively recognize the need to be free, and they sense the lack of the mystic communion with the earth that has been denied them. (See the 650th session in Chapter Thirteen.)", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第661节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "661", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0089", "zh": "不仅在意识层面上，而且在其他层面上，事实也是如此，你知道而且每个个体都知道，意识心相信太愚蠢又不理性的梦世界，其实是内我精心建构的，那种精确只有透过直觉才能获得。每一个个体都知道，这样一个辉煌的创造，存在于身为它源头的这个自己之外。", "en": "The fact also remains that on other levels but conscious ones, you know and every individual knows that the dream world that the conscious mind believes so foolish and irrational, is indeed constructed by the inner self with utmost care, with a precision known only by the intuitions. And each individual knows that such a splendid creation as this then exists beyond the self that was its origin.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第92节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "92", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0513", "zh": "任何时候，从事任意一种艺术的伟大艺术家，直觉的感觉到超乎特定性别的一种私人的人性。只要把你的本体与那你的性别视为相等，你就限制了个人和人类的潜能。每个人通常会发现较容易以一个男人或女人、一个女同性恋或男同性恋的身份运作，但每个人根本是双性的。双性暗含双亲性（Parenthood），就与它暗含男同性恋或女同性恋的关系一样。再次的，此地，性关系是爱的表现的一个自然的一部分，但它们并不是爱的表现的极限。", "en": "A great artist in any field or in any time instinctively feels a private personhood that is greater than the particular sexual identity. As long as you equate identity with your sexuality, you will limit the potentials of the individual and of the species. Each person will generally find it easier to operate as male or female, lesbian or homosexual, but each person is primarily bisexual. Bisexuality implies parenthood as much as it implies lesbian or homosexual relationships. Again, here, sexual encounters are a natural part of love’s expression, but they are not the limit of love’s expression.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第771节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "771", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "性别这条假界线", "note": "理性＝男、直觉＝女，是赛斯要拆掉的一套分工。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0510", "zh": "可是，你想象男人是攻击性的、积极的、有头脑逻辑的、发明性、外向的、文明之建造者。你把自我认同为男性。因此无意识似乎是女性了。而女性特征通常被认定为消极的、直觉性的、滋养的（nurturing：抚养）、创造性的、非发明性的、关心保持现状、不喜欢改变。同时，你们认为直觉性的成分相当吓人，好像它们能——未知的方式——爆炸而扰乱自己的模式。", "en": "You imagine, however, that the male is aggressive, active, logical-minded, inventive, outwardly oriented, a builder of civilizations. You identify the ego as male. The unconscious therefore seems to be female, and the feminine characteristics are usually given as passive, intuitive, nurturing, creative, uninventive, concerned with preserving the status quo, disliking change. At the same time, you consider the intuitive elements rather frightening, as if they can explode to disrupt known patterns, dash — in unknown ways.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第765节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "765", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0479", "zh": "我只不过在给你们所涉及的问题一个简短的概念，而我期待你们每个人以你们自己的方式去贯彻，去看看其联系，并且思考一下。那么，现在在你眼前你看到了什么？一个女人或一个男人？你看到违反了传统对性别或对意识概念的一列人与个性——违反了被传下来给你的所有概念，并且向你们每一个人挑战，要你们去找你们自己存在的实相。你的性别是一个焦点，只此而已。为你们那些需要听这句话的人，我现在要说：“一个女人就和一个男人一样的具有理性，一个男人就和一个女人一样的具有直觉。”你选择你的性别焦点是有理由的，那个理由与意识的弹性比你们目前所了解的要更有关系，它与积极和消极（侵略性和被动性）之真正本质有关，而你们已让你们自己忘了它……出生是一个积极的经验，而被动性是建立在对自然的侵略性之喜悦的认识上。被带着跑，你们每个人必须要对你自己非常有把握。以你们的话来说，要容许你自己享有现在所谓的一种被动之奢侈，你必须要对你自己的实相与力量之本质有信心，否则的话，被动性会令你害怕到骨子里。", "en": "Now I am simply giving you a brief idea of what is involved, and I expect each of you to follow through in your own way, to see the connections and think about them. And now, before you, what do you see? A woman or a man? You see a range of human being and personality that defies conventional ideas of sexuality or of consciousness — that defies all of the ideas that have been handed down to you, and that challenges you each to look for the reality of your own being. Your sexuality is a point of focus, and that is all. For those of you who need it said, I say it: A woman is as intellectual as a man. A man is as intuitive as a woman. You chose your sexual focus for a reason. The reason has more to do with the flexibility of consciousness than you presently understand. It has to do with the real nature of aggression and passivity,1 which you have allowed yourselves to forget … Birth is an aggressive experience. Passivity is based upon the joyful recognition of natural aggression. To be carried along, each of you must be very sure of yourself. To allow yourself what is now, in your terms, a luxury of passivity, you must have confidence in the nature of your own reality and strength. Otherwise passivity frightens you to the core.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第704节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "704", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0514", "zh": "在你们目前的构架里，因为男—女的专门化，你们采取男性的取向，暗示自我是男性，而心灵是女性。于是你们把很大的区分强加在你们自己身上，在期间的实际应用上，知性仿佛是与知觉分开的。而且你们设定了一种情况，在其中，敌对似乎适用于本来没有敌对的地方。当你们想到一个科学家，你们大多数会想到一个男人，一个知识分子，一个「客观的」思想者，他努力地不要感情用事，或与被检验或研究的主题认同。", "en": "In your present framework, because of the male-female specialization — the male orientation, the implication that the ego is male while the psyche is female — you force upon yourselves great divisions in which operationally the intellect seems separate from the intuitions, and you set up a situation in which opposites seem to apply where there are none. When you think of a scientist, the majority of you will think of a male, an intellectual, an “objective” thinker who takes great pains not to be emotional, or to identify with the subject being examined or studied.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第772节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "772", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0518", "zh": "那么。过度特定的性取向，反而映出意识里一个基本的区分。他不止把一个男人从他自己的直觉和感情，或一个女人从她的知性，分开到某个程度，而且也有效地提供了一个文明。在其中显得心智与心分开，而事实与天启隔离。到某种程度上，每个人都在同心灵打仗，因为一个人所有的特征必须被否定，除非它们符合那些对性认同来说被认为是正常的特征（for all of an individual’s human characteristics must be denied unless they fit in with those considered normal to the sexual identity.）。", "en": "The overly specific sexual orientation, then, reflects a basic division in consciousness. It not only separates a man from his own intuitions and emotions to some extent, or a woman from her own intellect, but it effectively provides a civilization in which mind and heart, fact and revelation, appear completely divorced. To some degree each person is at war with the psyche, for all of an individual’s human characteristics must be denied unless they fit in with those considered normal to the sexual identity.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第772节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "772", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0520", "zh": "你们试图把精神与感情的特征在性之间分割，强迫形成一种样板式的行为。再次的，具直觉性或某种艺术性天分的男人，常因而自认为同性恋者，不论他是或不是，因为他情感或精神的特征，似乎更适合女性而非男性。", "en": "You have tried to divide mental and emotional characteristics between the two sexes, forcing a stereotyped behavior. Again, the male who was intuitive or artistically gifted in certain ways often therefore considered himself homosexual, whether or not he was, because his emotional and mental characteristics seem to fit the female rather than the male sex.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第773节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "773", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0521", "zh": "具有那些超过那些被认为是女性兴趣的女人，也常处于同样的情形。可是，由于知性与情感被如此分开的考虑，因此她们表现直觉能力的尝试，常常变成「不合理的」行为。", "en": "The woman who had interests beyond those acceptable as feminine was often in the same position. Because the intellect and the emotions were considered so separately, however, attempts to express intuitive abilities often resulted in, and often do result in, “unreasonable” behavior.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第773节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "773", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B11", "title": "读赛斯，他自己要求你用直觉读", "note": "赛斯很清楚他在讲的东西超出线性语言的容量，所以他把怎么接这件事摆在内容前面。第249节他说他希望能把观念介绍给鲁柏，但经由直觉——这些观念随后就成为他智力的属性，帮助他们组合需要的字词。第82节他说一旦那一点被理解，其他所有资料就能同时以逻辑与直觉的方式被理解。他给的入口常常是一个具体的想象动作：想像那幅画，画里的距离不断往背景延伸却永远到不了画的后方，这也许能让你们对他那广阔的现在有一点直觉的了解——它有耐久性却不占用任何空间（第44节同段的另一句）；闲暇时想想你们自己的梦怎么构成，也许能凭直觉局部了解他的意思，因为梦里的距离没有尽头，却不占任何空间（第135节）；想想物质建构怎样变成你们环境的形状，也许就能凭直觉瞥见他在讲什么（第75节）。他还挑读者：菲利普若了解扩展的意义不在时间或空间、而在于价值完成，就能凭直觉理解到，当他说宇宙没有开始也没有结束时，与现有实相并没有矛盾（第95节）。第426节他坦白：这一切听起来复杂，只因为他们不得不用语言，他希望读者凭直觉理解。第170节则说明了他挑伙伴的标准：他要有的人格必须同时兼具理性与直觉，自我要平衡、健康、强壮，还要允许自己必然的自发行为与内在自由，这样的沟通才可能发生——太僵化或不够稳定的人格都不符合他的目标需求。对读者那一侧，他说这本书在某个程度就是写来帮助你们从一个不同的视角练习自己直觉性与精神性的能力（《未知的实相》卷二第743节）；他说他试着说出的观念几乎违抗知性的边缘，除非那知性被直觉的力量彻底加强，所以读这本书要用你的心智和你自己的直觉（《梦、进化与价值完成》第883节）；他希望书里那些精神练习能让你们跃过时间传统的架构，以统合的知性与直觉，感觉自己个人存在于那大到能包含所有时间片段的宽阔的现在里的那一部分（第884节）。念到具体的段落时，他说那问题本身就应当引动你的理智与直觉以另一种方式一起作用，哪怕只有一点点（第916节）；想象力在这里有很高的价值，因为它常能知觉到对理智而言不明显的统一——而你们已经把理智训练成只处理此时此地的证据（第918节）；让想象力作用于你们世界的一般事件上，至少瞥见一部分照亮那些事件的更大智慧，它会引导你直觉地对事件的源头与你们世界的源头有一个感受（第918节）。第461节他把代价讲得很明白：那份精简的态度会自然而然地让许多人得不到这些资料——他们需要它，能直觉地懂它，而且会好好用它。", "src": "《早期课》第2册第82节；第3册第95、135节；第6册第249节；第9册第426、461节；《未知的实相》卷二第743节；《梦、进化与价值完成》第883、884、916、918节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 82 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 95 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 135 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 249 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 426 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 461 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 743 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 883 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 884 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 916 节"}, {"n": 11, "id": null, "label": "第 918 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "他怎么把观念递过来", "note": "先给一个可以直觉进去的画面，再给论证。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0177", "zh": "我希望能够把观念介绍给鲁柏，但是经由直觉。然后这些观念就会成为他智力的属性，帮助我们组合我们需要的字词。", "en": "I hope to be able to introduce concepts to Ruburt, but intuitively. These will then become also a property of his intellect, and help us put the words together that we need.", "source": "早期课第6册 · 第249节", "year": "1967", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第6册", "session": "249", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0072", "zh": "一旦这一点能被理解，我们其他所有资料就可以同时用逻辑和直觉的方式被理解。的确，是这样的一本书该被编辑出来的时候了，而且我也的确建议当它被编辑出来的时候，你们请唐纳德·沃尔海姆先生写序。我们来详细讨论这件事。", "en": "Once this is understood, all the rest of our material can be seen in the light of both logic and intuition. It is, indeed, time that such a book be compiled, and I do suggest that when it is compiled you ask Mr. Wollheim to write an introduction. We will go into this more thoroughly as we progress.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第82节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "82", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0046", "zh": "不过，请记住，我们的宇宙充满它自己却不占用任何空间，还有我们那幅想像的画，画中的距离看起来在背景里一直不断延伸，却永远不会触及画的后方，这也许可以让你们对我们那广阔的现在有一些直觉的了解，它有着耐久性却不占用任何空间。", "en": "Remember however our universe that fulfills itself yet takes up no space, and our imaginary painting in which distance appears ever further in the background, while never touching the back of the painting, and this may give you some intuitive understanding of our spacious present that has duration, and yet takes up no space.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0124", "zh": "在这里要多做什么并不容易，只能给你们这一番陈述。如果你们要的话，闲暇时，可以想想你们自己的梦怎么构成，这样你们可能凭着直觉会局部了解我的意思，因为距离在梦中是没有尽头的，虽然你们可能会前进一点点；可是我们说过的这种距离不占任何空间。对于存在于一个行动之内，在电子上发生的距离，这近乎唤起一种对它的了解。", "en": "It is difficult here to do more than simply give you the statement. If you will, at your leisure, consider the makeup of your own dreams, you may partially and intuitively understand what I mean, for the distance in dreams is endless, though you may go but a little way; yet this distance as we have said, does not take up space. This comes close to evoking an understanding of distance as it occurs electrically, existing within an action.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第135节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "135", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0274", "zh": "这一切听起来很复杂，但只是因为我们不得不用语言来表达的缘故。我希望，凭直觉你们将能够理解它。与此同时，你们瞧，整体自己正在形成新的活动之线。它留下的那些架构可以被他人使用。（停顿。一如我先前所请求的。）", "en": "Now all of this sounds complicated, but only because we must deal in words. Intuitively, I hope, you will be able to understand it. In the meantime the overall self is forming new threads of activity, you see. The frameworks that it leaves behind can be used by others. (Pause. As I’d asked earlier.)", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第426节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "426", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0100", "zh": "菲利普应该读一读特别讲到宇宙法则，也就是宇宙的内在法则那几节，进而体会在所有的宇宙之内的这个宇宙既自发又耐久。重复那个冗长的讨论是开倒车，但是，就像内在宇宙有自发和耐久的属性，就像广阔的现在同时存在又涵盖所有的过去和所有的现在以及所有的未来，就像菲利普了解扩展的意义，不在于时间或空间，而在于价值完成，这样他就能凭直觉理解到，当我说宇宙没有开始也没有结束时，与现有的实相没有任何矛盾（contradiction）。（注：重新编译。）", "en": "Philip should read the sessions dealing particularly with the laws of the universe, that is with the inner laws of the universe, appreciating then the facts that this universe within all universes is spontaneous while having durability. It would be backtracking to repeat that long discussion, but as the inner universe has as its attributes spontaneity and durability, and as the spacious present is simultaneous while containing within it all pasts and all presents and all futures, and as Philip understands the meaning of expansion in terms not of time or of space but of value fulfillment, so will he intuitively then grasp that no contradiction occurs with actual reality when I say that there is no beginning and no end.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0066", "zh": "你们看得出来我们现在不过只是开始接触到一点皮毛而已。你们想想我说你们的物质建构，就我说过的心理形式而言，形成或变为你们环境的形状是什么意思，也许就能够凭借直觉瞥见我在讲的东西。", "en": "You can see that we have merely begun to scratch the surface here. You may, perhaps, glimpse what I mean in one way intuitively by considering what is meant when I say that your physical constructions form, or become the shape of, your environment in terms of what I have said about psychological form, period.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第75节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "75", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0137", "zh": "亲爱的殷斯翠姆博士，对于我会透过哪一种人格来讲话，你或许多少有些兴趣。我要的人格必须同时兼具理性与直觉，我要的自我是能平衡得很好，很健康、很强壮。还有，我要的人格必须能够允许它自己必然的自发行为与内在自由，以便这一类的沟通可以发生。没有基本稳定度的人格不符合我的目标需求，在信仰上和能力上太过僵化的人格，也不太符合我的目标需求。", "en": "All right now. You may be interested to some degree, dear Doctor Instream, in the sort of personality through whom I speak. I wanted a personality who was at the same time both intelligent and intuitional. I wanted an ego which was well balanced, healthy and strong. Yet I also wanted a personality which would allow itself the spontaneity necessary, and the inner freedom, so that such communications could take place. A personality without basic stability would not serve my purposes, and a personality that was too rigid in its beliefs and abilities would not serve my purposes well.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第170节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "170", "only_en": false}]}, {"label": "他要求读者怎么接", "note": "赛斯明说这些观念超出知性单独能接的范围。", "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0497", "zh": "它保持着星云似的朦胧，因为在意识上它并没被实现。实际上，我最多能做到的只是指出那些比较看不见的区域，去帮助你们探索你们自己意识的不同面。到某个程度，这本书是写来帮助你们由一个不同的视角练习你们自己直觉性与精神性的能力。", "en": "It remains nebulous because it is consciously unrealized. The best I can do is to point out areas that have been relatively invisible, to help you explore, actually, different facets of your own consciousness.2 To some extent this book has been written to help you exercise your own intuitive and mental capacities from a different viewpoint.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第743节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "743", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0581", "zh": "当你念那些段落时，那问题本身——“这些究竟是否是先前提到过的意识单位呢？”——就应引动了你的理智及你的直觉以另一种方式一起作用，纵使是只有些微的。当然，换言之，我希望在本书的这章及这部分专门谈这种主题，来激发你们的想象力及你们的智力。", "en": "As you read those passages the question itself—“Are these after all the units of consciousness referred to earlier?”—should have triggered your intellect and your intuition to work together, even if only slightly, in another way. In other words, of course, I hope to inspire both your imagination and your intelligence in this chapter and in this section of the book, devoted to such subject matter.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第916节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "916", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0582", "zh": "当我在那样做时，我也在试着引介给你们——至少直觉性的——一个更大的架构，在其中事件跨着你所知的实相。无论如何，我们要以非常可能看似有矛盾发生的议题来开始，因为你们对于一个事件的定义是如此简单，以致它们忽略了较大的分支——在一个整体而言结构与行动的更大统一里，那分支曾协调任何仿佛的矛盾。在此，你们的想象力会有很高的价值，因为它们常能知觉到对理智而言不明显的统一——你们已将理智训练成只去处理此时此地的证据。", "en": "While I am doing that I am also trying to introduce you, intuitively at least, to a larger framework, in which events straddle the reality that you know. Nevertheless, we will begin with issues in which it is very possible that contradictions may seem to occur, since your own definitions of an event are so simple that they ignore larger ramifications—ramifications that would reconcile any seeming contradictions in an overall greater unity of structure and action. Your imaginations will be of high value here, for they can often perceive unities that are not evident to the intellect—which you have trained to deal specifically with the evidence of the here and now.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第918节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "918", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0583", "zh": "你们言明的宇宙从那种间隔浮出，从一个其真实本质仍不为你们的定义所夺获的“主要事件”浮出——所以，在我们书里的有些地方，我可能会说一件你们已知的事件同时是真实而又不真实，或它既是迷思又是事实。而在如此做时，我希望引导你们对一种远远大于你们通常的真伪判断的事件有些心灵上的理解。那么，也许你会让你的想象力作用于你们世界的一般事件上，而至少瞥见一部分照亮那些事件的更大智慧，所以，想象力会引导你直觉的对事件的源头以及你们世界的源头有一个感受。我曾提到过的意识单位就是那种“事件”，而它们的确如所说的那样表现。换言之，意识单位也是存有，而你喜欢的话，也可说它是一切万有的片段体——力量与庄严的神圣片段，包含了如你所认识的所有的意识的力量，以你们的说法，它是个没有实质的浓缩物。", "en": "Your stated universe emerged out of that kind of interval, emerging from a master event whose true nature remains uncaptured by your definitions—so there will be places in our book where I may say that an event known to you is true and untrue at the same time, or that it is both myth and fact. And in so doing I hope to lead you toward some psychic comprehension of a kind of event far too large for your usual categories of true and false. [Perhaps], then, you will let your imaginations play upon the usual events of your world, and glimpse at least in part that greater brilliance that illuminates them, so that it leads you intuitively to a feeling for the source of events and the source of your world. The units of consciousness that I have mentioned are (underlined) that, and they do behave as I have said. They are also in other terms entities, fragments of All That Is, if you prefer—divine fragments of power and majesty, containing (pause) all of the powers of consciousness as you think of it, concentrations without substance in your terms.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第918节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "918", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0562", "zh": "在宇宙的开始之前，我们将假设一个全能的、创造性的来源和存在。（停顿。）我们希望能证明这神圣的主体性（subjectivity）现在仍在你们经验的世界里，就如在宇宙开始之前那样。再次的，我称这最初的主体性为一切万有。我正在试着说出一些观念，那是几乎违抗了知性的，除非那知性是彻底的为直觉的力量所强加。因此，在你读此书时，在你读此书时，你将需要用你的心智和你自己的直觉。", "en": "Before the beginning of the universe, we will postulate the existence of an omnipotent, creative source. (Pause.) We will hope to show that this divine subjectivity is as present in the world of your experience as it was before the beginning of the universe. Again, I refer to this original subjectivity as All That Is. I am making an attempt to verbalize concepts that almost defy the edges of the intellect, unless that intellect is thoroughly reinforced by the intuition’s strength. So you will need to use your mind and your own intuitions as you read this book.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第883节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "883", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0563", "zh": "我们依然称我们下一章为，把某些事件以顺序的形式罗列给你们。希望在此书其它部分的某些精神练习，会容许你们跃过传统的事件架构，而以统合的知性及直觉，感觉你自己个人存在于一个“宽阔的现在”的那部分，这宽阔的现在是大到能包含所有时间的片断的。", "en": "We will nevertheless call our next chapter “In the Beginning,” laying certain events out for you in serial form. I hope that in other portions of this book certain mental exercises will allow you to leap over the tradition of time’s framework and sense with the united intellect and intuitions your own individual part in a spacious present that is large enough to contain all of time’s segments.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第884节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "884", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0318", "zh": "然而这种态度会自然而然地使许多人得不到这些资料——他们需要它，能直觉地懂它，而且会好好用它。还会有别人，像鲁柏自己，像你，约瑟，会被基本资料里那些更充分的开展与论证所吸引。而这份作品的逻辑架构，仍将立基于此。", "en": "The attitude however could automatically make the material unavailable to many who need it, can understand it intuitively, and will use it well. There will be others, like Ruburt himself and like yourself, Joseph, who will be intrigued by those fuller developments and arguments given in the basic material. And upon these, again, the logical framework of the work will rest.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第461节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "461", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-085-e0010", "zh": "在某种程度上，你们可以在你们层面这么做，虽然程度很低，但是只能在一个维度的微小部分之内。也就是说，你们也许可以凭直觉感知或记得先前某个时刻，或是捕捉到先前某个时刻的视角影像，就像在照片中一，或在录音带中。你们可以通过影片回到过去的时光，捕捉到某一刻的视觉和听觉资料，甚至其后续明显可见的动作。通过你们那如此奇妙的电视——哈——观看比方说历史的某一刻，你们可以回顾很多已逝的历史性的时刻。", "en": "To some extent though to a much lesser degree you can do this on your own plane, but in a weak fraction of a dimension. That is, you can perhaps sense or remember an earlier moment intuitively or capture an earlier moment visually as in a photograph, or audibly as in a recording. You can through motion pictures refer back to past time, capturing the visual and auditory data of a moment and even the apparent motion of its sequence. Viewing through your so marvelous television—ha—a historical moment for example you can refer to much that has passed.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第14节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "14", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0122", "zh": "这是因为你由于性格使然，比较容易强调规律，但你在这些课里信任你的直觉，他也是。", "en": "This is because you are more apt to place stress upon regularity as a matter of your temperament, though you trust your intuitions in the sessions, as he does.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第134节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "134", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0246", "zh": "对他来说，有两个世界而不是一个，他不会直接将直觉应用在物质生活上。不过，他还是会帮助你发展内在的自由，让你可以应用在绘画上面。你自己的工作将会有一些变化， 你目前正朝着这样的方向前进。", "en": "There were two worlds to him instead of one, and he would not apply his intuitions to physical life directly. Nevertheless he helped develop your inner freedom so that you could apply it to your painting. There will be changes to come in your own work, and you are now reaching toward them.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第399节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "399", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0371", "zh": "因此，除了那些完全局限于这出戏的范围内的资料之外，他还有其他的资料来源。每个演员直觉地知道此点，而且在戏本身之中，已设有某些片段，已留有余地以便每个演员能休息而消除疲劳。在这种时候他的内在感官告知他他的其他角色，而他领悟到他是远超过在任一出戏剧中出现的自己。", "en": "(10:39. Long pause.) He has other sources of information, therefore, than those strictly given within the confines of the production. Each actor knows this instinctively, and there are periods set and allowed for within the play itself in which each actor retires in order to refresh himself. In these he is informed through the inner senses of his other roles, and he realizes that he is far more than the self appearing in any given play.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第521节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "521", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0380", "zh": "依照你的信念和发展，在你这方面也许有也许没有迷失感。现在我不一定是指理性的发展。理性应与情感和直觉携手同行，但如果理性太强烈地与情感和直觉作对，那么当新近得到自由的意识抓住理性对死后实相的概念，而不去面对它发现自己在其中的那个特定实相时，便可能有困难发生。换言之，意识能否认感觉，甚至试图强辩以否定它自己目前独立于肉体的情形。", "en": "There may or may not be disorientation on your part, according to your beliefs and development. Now I do not necessarily mean intellectual development. The intellect should go hand in hand with the emotions and intuitions, but if it pulls against these too strongly, difficulties can arise when the newly freed consciousness seizes upon its ideas about reality after death, rather than facing the particular reality in which it finds itself. It can deny feeling, in other words, and even attempt to argue itself out of its present independence from the body.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第536节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "536", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0395", "zh": "例如，暴风雨是非常具创造性的自然事件，虽然它们也能造成破坏。早期的人只能看到那破坏。有些人却直觉地了解到任何效果都是创造性的，不管它们表面看来如何，但很少人能说服他的同胞。", "en": "Storms, for example, are highly creative natural events, though they can also cause destruction. Early man could see only the destruction. Some intuitively understood that any effects are creative, despite their appearances, but few could convince their fellow men.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第568节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "568", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0401", "zh": "可以说，这喜悦延伸到将来，光明也照耀到过去，可能涵盖了比在那一刻能以具体方式表现的更大的范围。再来想象这个人由幻想落入一个出神状态或一个深睡中。（停顿良久）他可能看到对他非常具有象征性的喜悦或兴致勃勃的影像。逻辑上说，它们之间可能没多少关联，但在直觉上这关联是很清楚的。他现在比在幻想状态进入了深得多的精神体验，而可能有一连串的梦，在梦中他能表达他的喜悦而与他人分享。", "en": "The joy stretches out, so to speak, into the future, sheds also its light into the past, and may cover greater areas of expansion than could be shown in physical terms at that moment. Now imagine that our individual from his reverie falls either into a trance state or into a deep sleep. (Long pause.) He may see images that are highly symbolic to him of joy or exuberance. Logically there may be little connection between them, but intuitively the connections are clear. He now enters into his mental experiences far more deeply than in the reverie state, and may have a series of dream episodes in which he is able to express his joy and share it with others.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第571节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "571", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0413", "zh": "在一个主观层面上，在我每一生中我都充当教师与“说法者”。在几个直觉性很强的人生里，我是觉察这个事实的。你尚不了解意识内里的重要性。除了你在每生中的客观角色外，你的转世的挑战也涉及到你的梦境，那些在你所知的日常世界之下起落的创造性节奏。因此我在几生中以这种方式变成极熟练的说法者与教师，对比之下，这几生的表面生活则很无趣。", "en": "On a subjective level I acted as a teacher and a Speaker in each of my lives. In a few highly intuitive existences I was aware of this fact. You do not understand as yet the high importance of the underside of consciousness. Beside your objective role in each life, your reincarnational challenges also involve your dream states, rhythms of creativity that flow and ebb beneath the daily world you know. So I became highly proficient in this way as a Speaker and a teacher in several lives that were externally uninteresting by contrast.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第588节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "588", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0453", "zh": "你的母亲是在体验一个思想与直觉的加速，以及到目前为止一直被压抑的一大堆刺激。 她是十分清楚地在感知可能性，但把它们与实际的世界混淆了起来。不过，这只是当她实质的工作已完成后才发生的，而非譬如说，当方向的混淆会扰乱她自己任何必要的重要实质性目的时发生的。", "en": "… your mother is experiencing a mental and intuitive acceleration, a barrage of stimuli hereto withheld. She is perceiving probabilities quite clearly, but confusing them with the physical world of facts. This is only being done when her physical work is finished; not, for example, when disorientation could disrupt any necessary important physical purposes of her own.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第671节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "671", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0464", "zh": "在这儿的鲁柏选择了写作的架构，而坚守着它就如他一度坚守着教会一样的毫不动摇，但却又永远在寻找一个新的架构。有一阵子他把你理想化了，你的引导与力量成了他的架构。但当事情变得很明显，你也只是个人，而非一个架构时，他变得害怕了。当你鼓励他的神秘主义之浮现与表达时，那么，他感觉你不再能作为一个可涵盖他的架构。到那时，他仿佛威胁到你们生活的共同结构。他直觉的知道你也用艺术的创作作为你自己与神秘的表现之间的一个缓冲。", "en": "(Intently:) Ruburt here chose the writing structure, and has stuck to it as unswervingly as he once stuck to the church, yet always seeking a new framework. For a while he idealized you. Your guidance and strength were his framework. When it became apparent that you were also human, and not a framework, he became frightened. When you encouraged the emergence and expression of his mysticism, then you could no longer act, he felt, as a framework to contain it. By then it seemed to threaten the joint structure of your lives. He knew intuitively that you also used artistic creation as a buffer between yourself and mystical expression.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第679节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "679", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0490", "zh": "厄尔·威廉斯及山姆·盖瑞特是对等人物。对我的读者而言，这些名字毫无意义，但在每个例子里，所提到的关系指明了内在的了解与联系，这同样的实相也出现在你们每个的生命里。威尔·佩托斯基及班·费恩是对等人物。威尔（即参与第七二九节的威廉之短名）是个非常聪明的年轻人——他引以为豪，虽然他很努力的表示他跟别人是一样的。在另一方面，班完全信任他自己的直觉，而且依赖着它，但却多少害怕他自己充沛的精力，在许多方面他还是个孩于，而绝对的自发。", "en": "Earl (Williams) and Sam (Garret) are counterparts. To my readers these names mean nothing. Yet in each case the relationships noted indicate inner realizations and connections. The same realities appear in each of your lives. Will Petrosky and Ben (Fein) are counterparts. Will (who, incidentally, witnessed the 729th session) is a very intellectual young man — proud of it, though he goes to great effort to show he is one of the boys. On the other hand, Ben Fein trusts his intuitions fully, and relies upon them, yet to some extent fears his own great energy. In many respects he is a child, and utterly spontaneous.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第732节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "732", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0516", "zh": "到某个程度，有些科学界的人，设法融合所谓的女性与男性的特征。当他们如此做时，似乎敌对和矛盾消失了。不论到什么程度，他们都比他们当代的人更不容许性角色使他们在心理盲目。因此他们比较容易结合理性和情感，知觉与知性，而在如此做时，他们发明了能调和以前的矛盾的理论。他们统合、拓展、创造，而非分化。", "en": "To an extent, some people in the sciences manage to blend the so-called female and male characteristics. When they do so, seeming oppositions and contradictions disappear. To whatever degree, more than their contemporaries, they do not allow sexual roles to blind them psychologically. Therefore they are more apt to combine reason and emotion, intuitions and intellect, and in so doing invent theories that reconcile previous contradictions. They unify, expand, and create, rather than diversify.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第772节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "772", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0571", "zh": "与其说这种发展超过了人的能力，不如说以人目前的立足点而言，这涉及了实际上不可能做到的操纵。相对的说，理论上，人们可以在一眨眼移到一个较优越的立足点，但目前我们必须大半用比喻。那些比喻也许可以引导你、鲁柏或少数其它人到一个更有利的观点，以使某种跃进变得可能——但，你明白吗？那些跃进不只是知性上的跃进，也是意志与直觉的跃进，全都融合并且集中在一起。", "en": "It is not [so much] that such developments are beyond man’s capacity as it is that they involve manipulations impossible to make for all practical purposes, from his present standpoint. He could theoretically move to a better vantage point in the twinkling of an eye, relatively speaking, but for now we must largely use analogies. Those analogies may lead you or Ruburt, or a few others, to a more advantageous vantage point, so that certain leaps become possible—but those leaps, you see, are not just leaps of intellect but of will and intuition alike, fused and focused.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第900节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "900", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0585", "zh": "我并不想变得卷入于名词的混淆里，按照我们上一节的私人课，心智的力量远远大过那些一般被指派给单单的理性思维力量。举例来说，理性的推理用过火了，那实际上能限制智能的实际利用，因而使得心智的一些领域变得迟钝了。再次的，以一种说法，协助者代表了心智作用真正的能力，那种在直觉与心智活动两者背后的即刻理解。那么，你是在与广阔的理智——知晓者（knower）——打交道。", "en": "(Long pause, one of many in a much slower delivery.) I do not want to become involved in a confusion of terms. The mind’s powers are far greater than those generally assigned to rational thought alone, as per our last (private) sessions. Rational reasoning, overdone, can for example actually limit practical use of the intellect’s faculties, and therefore serve to dim some of the mind’s scope. In a fashion, again, Helper represents the true capacity of the mind’s functioning, the kind of instant comprehension that is behind both the intuitions and the intellect’s activities. You are dealing, then, with the spacious intellect, the knower.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第922节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "922", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-085-e0606", "zh": "那么，小说的点子是来自过去和未来的事件，虽然你很快就会追上了那些未来事件。你的心智直觉地组织所有那些数据，以一种全新的方式将它放到一起。有时当这种事件发生，当预知性的板机被实质地发动时，它甚至没能被认出来，因为它在事前太早就发生了。（对我说。）你是以一种具创意的方式组织精神的和实质的事件。在这例子里涉及了一篇小说，因为，虽然那观念强烈地涉及了图像，却延伸过一段时间，而使得文字描述变得必要。", "en": "The idea, then, of the novel came from past and future events, though you were to catch up with those future events very quickly. Your mind intuitively organized all of that material, and put it together in a completely new fashion. Sometimes when such events occur, the precognitive trigger is not even recognized when it is encountered physically, because it happens too far ahead of time. (To me:) You organize mental and physical events in a creative manner. In this case a novel was involved because the concept, while strongly involving images, carried a time span that would make narrative necessary.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第13节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "13", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 14}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 14}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 14}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 13}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 12}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 10}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 10}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 10}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 9}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 9}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 9}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 9}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 6}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 6}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 6}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 5}, {"name": "健康之道", "count": 3}, {"name": "早期课第6册", "count": 2}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 11, "quotes": 161, "reading": 15, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 3}};
